:"$remainingCount na character ang natitira",C3:"% is used to represent a percentage. This is displayed next to an input field to indicate the unit of measurement for that field is a percentage.",tG:"% of the way to being a CircleBorder that is ",S3:"'. Valid formats include YYYY, YYYY-MM, YYYY-MM-DD, YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ, or YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss\xb1hh:mm.",G6:". Please review and correct the addresses in your file before re-importing.",uS:"A KMZ file must contain a KML file. Ensure the file contains a .kml file and try again.",Z5:"A brief description of the Google Timelapse feature described at https://blog.google/products/earth/new-imagery-google-earth-timelapse-videos/.",Ei:"A button that allows the user to sign up to try the Google Earth 'Professional Advanced' plan. The button links to a page where the user can start a new project.",wM:"A button that allows the user to sign up to try the Google Earth 'Professional' plan. The button links to a page where the user can start a new project.",tV:"A dropdown option in the layer details inspector panel that when selected, will make all features in the layer share the same style.",oE:"A feature of the 'Standard' Earth plan, shown in a bulleted list of features. 'imagery' refers to satellite and aerial imagery.",B1:"A header for a menu section that contains tools that allow users to analyze their site, such as contours, aspect, and slope analysis.",OH:"A hint that lets Screen Reader users that they must press to enter Search mode.",Gp:"A label for a button in a confirmation dialog that asks the user if they want to start the design tool input process again.  The button will start the process over, discarding the user's last saved site and inputs.",M0:"A label for a text field that allows the user to edit the name of a building.",Mq:"A label for an invisible button placed on top of a StreetView Arrow. Used to make the arrows more accessible via Screen Readers.",Pd:"A label indiating that the user has not selected any building use types for design generation.",TJ:"A map feature category that controls whether Voyager stories are displayed on the map.",Ng:"A map feature category that controls whether or not real-time atmospheric clouds are shown on the globe at higher altitudes. The clouds are updated throughout the day to reflect the current weather.",cc:"A map feature category that includes all possible feature categories.",Om:"A map feature category that includes bodies of water, such as an ocean, sea or lake.",ZX:'A member of the group of "Landscape" features that includes only natural features such as a mountain or island, not those made by humans. This category includes both the "Landcover" and "Terrain" categories.',jO:'A member of the group of "Landscape" features that includes those that are made by humans rather than natural. This includes buildings and other structures such as bridges.  It also includes the notion of a "built up area".',V_:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes all types of parks.',A1:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places for medical treatment such as clinics and hospitals.',gj:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places of worship, such as a church, mosque or temple.',eZ:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places that are primarily car rental related, such as car rental agencies and car service locations.',c4:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places that are primarily food and drink related, such as restaurants, bars, cafes, and bakeries.',Vz:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places that are primarily gas station related, such as gas stations, convenience stores, and car wash.',J4:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places that are primarily lodging related, such as hotels, motels, and bed and breakfasts.',I8:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes places that would attract visitors, such as museums, amusement parks or zoos.',oj:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes sports facilities such as a stadium or ballpark.',fS:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes various educational institutions, including those for children as well as universities.',ZY:'A member of the group of "Place" features that includes various types of shopping facilities, including malls, department stores and outlet stores.',mh:'A member of the group of "Place" features that primarily consists of business establishments.',yP:'A member of the group of "Place" features that primarily includes government offices and buildings.',cn:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes all the smaller local roads.',Ab:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes lanes on road networks.',Do:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes major surface streets ("arterials") that are not considered highways.',qO:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes only major highways.  This category includes controlled access highways as well as major highway sections that do not have controlled access.',TH:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes only those highways with limited cross street access, such as an American freeway, German autobahn or French autoroute.',w_:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes small, local roads.',ec:'A member of the group of "Roads" features that includes trails and walkways.',YD:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes airports.',v2:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes all types of transit station, including Rail Stations, Bus Stops, Airports and Ferry Terminals.',P1:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes collections of transit route lines in some areas.',wn:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes ferry route lines in some areas.',eC:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes ferry terminals.',Ag:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes official stop locations for auto buses.',zi:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes railway and metro or subway stations.',EB:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes railway routes and stops in some areas.',jh:'A member of the group of "Transit" features that includes transit route lines in some areas.',Bx:'A member of the group of "administrative" map feature categories that includes international borders and the names of countries.',zD:'A member of the group of "administrative" map feature categories that includes local municipalities such as Cities and Towns, as ell as some large administrative areas within a city, such as an arrondissement (Paris) or borough (New York).',Nz:'A member of the group of "administrative" map feature categories that includes smaller areas within a City or Town, for example "Midtown" in New York\'s borough of Manhattan, or "Faubourg St. Germain" within Paris\' 7th arrondissement.',hS:'A member of the group of "administrative" map feature categories that includes the borders and names of primary administrative units within a country, such as states (America), provinces (Canada), regioni (Italy).',BL:'A member of the group of "administrative" map feature categories that is intended to refer to the boundaries of individual parcels of land, or "lots".',T1:'A member of the group of natural "Landscape" features that includes elements of the earth\'s topography including mountains and valleys.',fH:'A member of the group of natural "Landscape" features that includes landcover types such as grasslands, tundras, deserts, ice, shrubs, sand, etc.',Zh:"A menu option for a sub-menu of file import related options",CL:'A menu option in the File/Open submenu that allows the user to see and open their Google My Maps ("My Maps" is the product name) projects stored in Google Drive.',jZ:"A menu option that allows the user to activate or deactivate the Historical Imagery feature on the map.",Up:"A menu option that allows the user to activate the Historical Imagery feature on the map.",QQ:"A menu option that allows the user to add a data layer to the selected project.",Gs:"A menu option that allows the user to add a folder in the selected project.",eg:"A menu option that allows the user to add a folder to the project.",bX:"A menu option that allows the user to add a path or polygon in the selected project.",Ll:"A menu option that allows the user to add a placemark in the selected project.",dk:"A menu option that allows the user to add a slide (like a slide in a presentation) to a project.",R5:"A menu option that allows the user to add a tile overlay on the map.",zX:"A menu option that allows the user to add measurement lines in the selected project.",v:"A menu option that allows the user to adjust the map view to fit the selected feature.",DY:"A menu option that allows the user to attach the current map view.",Ee:"A menu option that allows the user to begin selecting features in the current project using checkboxes.",TD:"A menu option that allows the user to bring the selected layer to the back in terms of draw order. Draw order defines how features are stacked on the map. Features with higher draw order values are drawn on top of features with lower draw order values.",wl:"A menu option that allows the user to bring the selected layer to the front in terms of draw order. Draw order defines how features are stacked on the map. Features with higher draw order values are drawn on top of features with lower draw order values.",j_:"A menu option that allows the user to copy a folder (and its contents).",Ff:"A menu option that allows the user to copy a single feature.",u5:"A menu option that allows the user to copy all selected features.",iI:"A menu option that allows the user to copy multiple features.",m:"A menu option that allows the user to copy the selected text or feature.",Fz:"A menu option that allows the user to create a new Google Earth map.",op:"A menu option that allows the user to create a new Google Earth site study.",Gl:"A menu option that allows the user to create a new KML file on local device.",IT:"A menu option that allows the user to de-select all text or features.",bJ:"A menu option that allows the user to deactivate the Historical Imagery feature on the map.",WF:"A menu option that allows the user to duplicate the selected project.",QL:"A menu option that allows the user to export the selected file as a KML file.",rh:"A menu option that allows the user to hide the latitude/longitude gridlines on the map.",pg:"A menu option that allows the user to import a KML or KMZ file from the device.",nq:"A menu option that allows the user to import a KML or KMZ file.",lc:"A menu option that allows the user to open a local KML file.",O1:"A menu option that allows the user to open an existing KML file.",E5:"A menu option that allows the user to open the Google Earth channel in YouTube in a browser window.",XP:"A menu option that allows the user to redo their last action.",Op:"A menu option that allows the user to select a Google Drive KML or KMZ file to import into a Google Earth Project.",sb:"A menu option that allows the user to select a Google Drive file to import into a newly created Google Earth Drive project.",IB:"A menu option that allows the user to select all text or features.",pu:"A menu option that allows the user to show the latitude/longitude gridlines on the map.",F:'A menu option that allows the user to start presenting the feature or project they\'re currently viewing in presentation mode. "Present" here is a verb, and has the sense of a slide deck..',rI:"A menu option that allows the user to undo their last action.",pE:"A menu option that allows the user to upload a local file to import into a Google Earth Project.",GE:"A menu option that allows the user to view the basemap settings dialog.",LV:"A menu option that enters Street View at the point the camera is looking at",W4:"A menu option that flies the user to a view of the entire Earth from space.",pv:"A menu option that opens an editor for the selected layer.",dw:"A menu option that opens the 'Community Forum' in a browser window.",Qa:"A menu option that opens the 'Documentation' Help Center in a browser window.",by:"A menu option that opens the Earth release notes page in a new browser window.",PV:"A menu option that resets the 3D view so that north is up.",ZI:"A menu option that resets the 3D view so that the camera is looking straight down at the ground and north is up.",ol:"A menu option that resets the 3D view so that the camera is looking straight down at the ground.",M7:'A menu option that shows the user a "About Google Earth" dialog.',KS:'A menu option that shows the user a "Command Palette" dialog.',aQ:'A menu option that shows the user a "Help" dialog.',c8:'A menu option that shows the user a "Keyboard Shortcuts" dialog.',vF:'A menu option that shows the user the "Feedback" dialog.',Ti:'A menu option that shows the user the "Settings" dialog.',wS:"A menu option that toggles between a static top-down view and a tilted view orbiting around the center of the current viewport.",hE:"A menu option within the File/Open submenu that lets the user pick a local KML/KMZ file to load. It does not repeat Open since it is the name of the submenu.",E2:"A menu option within the Import file to project menu that allows the user to select a Google Drive file to import into a Google Earth Project.",yj:"A menu option within the Import file to project menu that allows the user to upload a local file to import into a Google Earth Project.",mA:"A message notifying the user the filters they used don't have any matching results.",q1:"A message prompting the user to switch to a 2D view to refresh the data table.",lL:"A message prompting the user to zoom in because the data has been thinned because the field of view is too broad to show all the data at once.",Hr:"A message saying that the Historical Imagery feature needs to be disabled in order to enable another feature. This may appear for example as a tooltip, or an alternative subtitle for a switch.",T6:"A message shown at the top of a status card, which shows the statuses of the user's ongoing and failed designs, that the user has designs that are still undergoing generation.",Uy:"A message shown in a data table when more Google Earth projects are in the process of being loaded.  This message will disappear once the loading operation is complete.",G2:"A message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window when the user has an outdated map project open.",Lg:"A message shown to the user to alert them that a feature is only supported on web environments.",Gv:"A message to users who attempt to view an Earth Design project but who are not in the experiment group. The message will be displayed as text in a panel.",oz:"A new Google Earth home screen is coming soon",ts:"A short description of the Pinned Projects dialog for the productivity view.",G_:"A short description of the Pinned Projects dialog for the streamlined view.",Oj:"A short name for the Cut and fill layer type, shown in a list of document operations.",ay:"A short text for a toast indicating to the user that Google Earth had got an issue with graphics context and needs a restart.",PR:"A short text label indicating that a document should be stored in Google Drive.",zV:"A small label indicating that the current project has been automatically saved on Google Drive. Please, use very short translation.",wU:"A text description in a confirmation dialog that asks the user if they want to start the design tool input process again.",uE:"A text label indicating that a document should be stored on the user's local device (i.e. on their mobile device or in their local browser storage).",PL:"A text title of a confirmation dialog that asks the user if they want to start the design tool input process again.",I7:"A toast message informing the user that the device has restored internet connection.",E4:"A toast message informing the user that the device lost internet connection.",VG:"A toast to notify the user that the feature could not be pasted because the user is not signed in.",Eq:"A tooltip for the button that activates the navigation controls view.",mO:"A tooltip notifying the user that tapping this button will trigger the account details and settings.",Zl:"A tooltip notifying the user that tapping this button will trigger the account details.",Wa:"A tooltip or toast notifying the user about an authentication error, suggesting to try switching accounts.",uM:"A tooltip that explains the percent loaded indicator in the status bar.",AP:"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/",HK:"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_",Jp:"ADVANCED_MEASUREMENTS_ELEVATION_PROFILE_ENABLED",Hi:"Access data layers for electric vehicles, multi-dwelling units, rooftop reflectivity, tree canopy, and much more",uD:"Access new data layers for household income and land surface temperature",ng:"Access the data catalog anytime to explore and add more layers.",Um:"Action text of a toast that lets the user navigate to the Android Play Store.",Pa:"Action that is shown in an info card when a user is in polygon selection mode when attempting to create an area filter but there are no polygons in the current project. Area filters are used to filter data in a data layer based on a user defined area or polygon.",Dw:"Action that is shown in an info card when a user is in polygon selection mode when attempting to create or generate a cut and fill analysis but there are no polygons in the current project. This prompts users to create a polygon by drawing it and save it to the project. Cut and fill analysis refers to the process of calculating the volume of earth that needs to be moved to create a level surface.",tT:"Action that is shown in an info card when a user is in polygon selection mode when attempting to create or generate a slope analysis but there are no polygons in the current project. This prompts users to create a polygon by drawing it and save it to the project. Slopes refer to the steepness of the terrain.",n4:"Action that is shown in an info card when a user is in polygon selection mode when attempting to create or generate an aspect analysis but there are no polygons in the current project. This prompts users to create a polygon by drawing it and save it to the project. Aspect refers to the direction a slope is facing.",Gr:"Action that is shown in an info card when a user is in polygon selection mode when attempting to create or generate contours but there are no polygons in the current project. This prompts users to create a polygon by drawing it and save it to the project. Contours refer to lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain.",HD:"Activate to display map navigation controls on the screen",Rd:"Activate your upgraded Google Earth plan.",Wu:"Activate your upgraded plan with a Google Cloud project",RO:"Add Residential or Hotel use types to see advanced use type settings.",j3:"Add a new group of floors within this part of the building type. Each floor group shares the same use types and floor-to-floor height.",sY:"Add and style individual features to highlight specific areas (up to 10k)",LA:"Add at least two classes to your layer. Then, place sample points to train the model.",hH:"Add basement parking to existing and new building types.",r_:"Add building types for your development program. Include as many as you'd like, then customize use type and dimensions.",fc:"Add features, map view, or files to refine your prompt",Xj:"Add these to see how you can reduce carbon emissions over the next 10 years.",g1:"Add use type percentage refers to adding an additional constraint to the site target based on an existing use type.",aZ:"Add zoning requirement refers to adding an additional zoning requirement to a land parcel.",ZN:"Adding financial and energy details help make solar designs more accurate. Estimates are pre-filled based on your area. You can adjust them now or make changes later.",g4:"Adding zoning requirements will help ensure that your designs are feasible.",n9:"Adjust graphics settings to optimize app performance",HA:"After processing, the file did not contain any features. This may be because the file contained only features that are not supported by the selected output format.",cH:"All area units and measurements will default to this unit.",EZ:"All borders, labels, places, roads, transit, landmarks and water.",zj:"All distance units and measurements will default to this unit.",SV:"All slope units and measurements will default to this unit.",bG:"All: Sell all energy generated from solar",Iw:"Also known as lifetime savings, it represents the total savings from investing in the solar system over its lifespan - 25 years.",DS:"Altitude of the camera relative to sea level",hp:"An accessibility label for the Screen Reader to notify the user they are focusing the bottom sheet drag handle area, in a collapsed state",CN:"An accessibility label for the Screen Reader to notify the user they are focusing the bottom sheet drag handle area, in an expanded state",RU:"An accessibility label for the menu that will sort a list of items by some value.",XZ:"An accessibility label for the price of the Professional and Professional Advanced plan during the initial experimental period, used to make the price more clear to screen readers.",S2:"An accessibility tooltip to let the user know if they activate this button, the bottom sheet will collapse",_a:"An accessibility tooltip to let the user know if they activate this button, the bottom sheet will expand",SR:"An error occurred during validation. Please try again.",hB:"An error occurred while creating inputs. Try again or reload the page.",dK:"An error occurred while discarding inputs. Try again or reload the page.",H5:"An error occurred while extracting features from the file. You may find more details in the full error log.",jW:"An error occurred while starting over. Try again or reload the page.",NA:"An option in a dropdown menu for selecting the unit type for the program targets of a site or parcel. These unit type options include floor area ratio (FAR) or gross floor area (e.g. sq ft or sq m).",r1:"An option in a dropdown menu for selecting the unit type for the program targets of a site or parcel. These unit type options include floor area ratio (FAR) or gross floor area (e.g. sq ft or sq m). Gross means total floor area in this context.",aJ:'An overall map feature category that includes all "Place" features, such as businesses, schools, government buildings and so forth.',tF:'An overall map feature category that includes all "administrative" features such as borders (national and internal), and the names of towns, cities and neighborhoods.',MG:"An overall map feature category that includes all types of public transit features, including transit lines, stations and airports.",mB:"An overall map feature category that includes all types of roadways from super-highways to local streets.",bN:'An overall map feature category that includes features that appear to be part of the land as one can see it, or "landscape". This includes land formations, mountain peaks, beaches, islands, etc., as well as elements of the built-up human environment such as building outlines, etc.',xy:"Announcements about product and feature updates from Google Earth",Td:"Area is self-intersected. Create separate parcels instead.",vI:"Artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI / ML)",KE:"Ask Google Earth has been updated. To continue using, please create a new map.",xQ:"Ask Google Earth to help you explore the map, get insights, and work faster",o2:"Ask for edit access to collaborate and make changes.",WP:"Assess your site for real estate development or solar and generate design options for feasibility.",_k:"Asset valuation (banking, insurance, credit risk)",yO:"Attempted to change a read-only map field",w8:"Authentication error. Please try switching accounts.",JM:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_AREA_FILTER",ZC:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_BILLING_SETTINGS",lP:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_DEBUG_SETTINGS",uA:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_DESIGN_INPUT_MODE_CHOOSER",cS:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_EXPLORE_PROMO_DIALOG",xH:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_HOMESCREEN_PROMO",dz:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_HOMESCREEN_STORAGE_SUMMARY",xx:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_LAYERS_DIALOG_DETAILS_VIEW",XO:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_LAYERS_DIALOG_GRID_VIEW",YE:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_LAYERS_INSPECTOR_PANEL",V5:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_NEW_BUILD_DESIGN_INPUT_SITE_TAB_ZONING",hu:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_ON_DEMAND_CONTOUR_ANALYSIS",JD:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_PLAN_CHIP",Gw:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_SITE_SELECTION",vP:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_SOLAR_DESIGN_INPUT_SITE_TAB",Sc:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_STANDARD_USER_PROMO_BANNER",z1:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_UNSPECIFIED",rC:"BILLING_UPGRADE_DIALOG_SOURCE_VIEW_USER_IMPORTED_LAYER",if:"BUILTENV_VIEW_PRESET_ON_DEMAND_FETCHING_ENABLED",Gq:"BUILTENV_VIEW_PRESET_SUNLIGHT_HOURS_ENABLED",Og:"BUILT_ENV_CREATE_MORE_DESIGNS_LIKE_THIS_ENABLED",BS:"BUILT_ENV_DISABLE_DESIGN_GENERATION_ENABLED",RA:"Badge (text in a blue rounded rectangle) appended to menu entries to indicate a new functionality.",yY:"Banner text that asks the user to update their user profile with information about their job or role in order to improve Earth. This banner will be occasionally shown when users open Earth.",nF:"Banner text that informs the user that they have been added as a user to an Earth plan. This text is shown in the settings panel.",zl:"Banner text that informs the user that they have been added as a user to more than one Earth premium plan.",sk:"Banner text that prompts the user to share information about their job or role to improve Earth.",WD:"Basemap settings are only visible to you and will not be shared with this project",LT:"Basement floor group editing is disabled when the basement parking strategy is disabled and basement parking floor groups are present. Currently, basement floor groups will be not generated for this building type.",I0:"Basement floors are restricted to only parking use types.",JP:"Body of a dialog that asks the user to rename their project before sharing it.",m5:"Body of a dialog that asks the user to rename their untitled map before sharing it.",d7:"Body text for a banner that informs the user that they are in a Google Cloud Platform project that grants them access to an Earth premium plan. This describes additional features that would be enabled. 'site' refers to geographic areas for real estate development. GCP does not need to be translated.",K6:"Body text for a sheet or dialog that asks the user to specify where to export a site study design, whether to a new Earth map or a pre-existing Earth map. It indicates that it can be shown alongside other Earth map features (e.g. placemarks, paths, polygons, slides, etc.) and layers.",U4:"Body text for a sheet or dialog that asks the user to specify where to start design generation, whether to a new Drive project or a pre-existing project",sf:"Body text for an Earth inline promotion card. This text is meant to prompt users to complete a survey in Earth about their job or role and their use of Earth.",Zw:"Body text in a dialog that appears after the first time a user tries to share their project via Drive.",Vn:"Body text in a dialog that appears after the first time a user tries to share their project via Drive. This line appears above the user's photo and name.",tI:"Body text of a card shown when there is an error from fetching data for the selected layer feature.",Kb:"Body text of a view that promotes the overhead satellite imagery search feature in the Earth AI assistant.",p_:"Body text to promote the Earth AI assistant button when it is first introduced to the user.",B4:"Body text to promote the Earth data catalog button when it is first introduced to the user. This is shown in the coachcard, under the data catalog button, only when a user enters the data catalog from a source that is not the toolbar.",s:"Boolean value should be empty. Found instead: ",S7:"Brainstorm, create custom maps, and ask follow-ups to clarify your needs",zY:"Brief description of what the Import File to Map Project button does",PF:"Brief description of what the New Local KML file button does. Note: KML stands for Keyhole Markup Language. It should not be translated, unless the language has another abbreviation for KML.",Ph:"Brief description of what the New Map Project button does. In Drive means that it is stored in Google Drive.",xR:"Brief description of what the Open Local KML file button does",g:"Brief label that indicates that the features being edited have different values for a particular style (icon, color, etc.).",jw:"Bring your 3D design into an Earth map and present it alongside other map layers.",GC:"Bring your browser KML file data to an Earth map",MC:"Button label for adding a unit mix for a buidling use type. A building use type is a type of building (e.g. residential, hotel). The unit mix refers to the percentage of different types of residential units in a building. For example, a building may have 10% one bedroom units, 40% two bedroom units, and 50% three bedroom units. Clicking this button will give users the option to add another unit mix for a use type.",fd:"Button label for exporting a document as a KML file. This button is shown in a dialog that warns the user that some layers and features cannot be exported as a KML file.",Z0:"Button label for resetting the zoning requirement inputs for a parcel to the default values.",ap:"Button label inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to create a new cloud project.",FS:"Button label inviting user to switch to a view that shows them their local KML files, as opposed to their Google Drive projects.",hA:"Button label to open the settings page to activate a Earth plan.",pk:"Button text for a button in an inline banner card on the buildings tab of the generate designs workflow. This button takes the user to parking tab of the workflow.",Sg:"Button text for a button in an inline banner card on the parking tab of the generate designs workflow. This button takes the user to buildings tab of the workflow.",JA:"Button text for adding classes to a classification layer. Classification layers use AI to categorize the basemap into different classes based on user-defined sample points. Add classes allows the user to define sample points.",h3:"Button text for choosing to delete just this attribute from the current feature",EL:"Button text for choosing to delete the given attribute key across all the features in the current document",Z1:"Button text for removing a floor group from a building type in the edit building type dialog.",J:"Button text for requesting access to a project.",uG:"Button text indicating a point will be added when the button is pressed. Used for the measure tool.",qa:"Button text indicating a selection is made at the position as marked on the map when the button is pressed. Used for the measure tool.",K7:"Button text or tooltip indicating a shape will be close by adding a point when the button is pressed. Used for the measure tool.",cy:"Button text that prompts the user to take a survey about whether they are a professional, consumer, or other user, and for what job or role they use Earth. This banner will be occasionally shown when users open Earth.",k_:"Button that allows the user to confirm that they want to deselect their current Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project. GCP does not need to be translated.",MD:"Button that allows the user to confirm that they want to leave their current Earth subscription plan.",H4:"Button that opens the Data Catalog dialog in Google Earth. Used in various promotion cards.",y4:"Button to confirm that the user wants to switch their Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project. The selected GCP project determines the selected Earth subscription plan. GCP does not need to be translated.",H2:"By default, we'll estimate your site's energy usage based on size and location. Check the checkbox to enter your own assumptions from your utility bill.",TY:"By providing feedback on your prompt, Google may review and use your feedback, your prompt and our response to your prompt. This data will be associated with your Google account for two weeks.",_h:"By using electrified heating you reduce your site\u2019s energy usage by ",Dh:"CANT_ADD_FEATURE_DUE_TO_FEATURE_COUNT_LIMIT",P2:"CONTENT_CREATION_MOBILE_ADD_PHOTOS_ENABLED",u4:"CONTENT_CREATION_MOBILE_COLLAPSED_DOCUMENT_VIEW_ENABLED",xT:"CONTENT_CREATION_MOBILE_PROPERTY_EDITOR_ENABLED",vt:"CREATE_DOCUMENTS_AS_MODEL_VERSION_V2_ENABLED",Pb:"CREATE_DOCUMENTS_AS_MODEL_VERSION_V3_ENABLED",nQ:"CREATE_DOCUMENTS_AS_MODEL_VERSION_V4_ENABLED",xP:"Called rasterize() with a different number of canvases and pictures.",rz:"Cannot extract a file path from a URI with a fragment component",ll:"Cannot extract a file path from a URI with a query component",BB:"Cannot extract a non-Windows file path from a file URI with an authority",xS:"Cannot fire new event. Controller is already firing an event",FD:"Caution message that the measure tool is best used with the globe in 2D mode, rather than 3D. Appears as a tooltip and also as a toast.",i8:"Changing GCP projects may impact access to paid features",M9:"Checkbox on the solar design input form that will signal whether or not design generation should estimate the energy usage of the site or use the user's provided values. When enabled, it will use the user's provided values.",dV:"Choose data layers to add to your project.",y8:"Choose what kind of design project you want to create, then select your site.",yQ:"Clears the list of trusted and untrusted domains for loading KML content",Ys:"Click a highlighted street to enter Street View.",Pf:"Click points on the map to draw a path or polygon",e1:"Click points on the map to measure distances and area",eR:"Click refresh to see your latest settings",rZ:"Clickable text shown alongside the area description footnote that links to a relevant help center article.",Xf:"Clickable text shown below the area description summary that expands the view to show a longer, more detailed description.",Ec:"Clickable text shown below the area description that minimizes the view to only show a brief area description summary.",_s:"Clickable text that is shown in the Area Description view when there is an error fetching the description. Clicking it re-fetches the description.",vY:"Clickable text that opens a terms and privacy page about the Earth AI assistant. It is shown after the 'earthMateFeedbackDisclaimer' text.",_c:"CodedBufferReader encountered an embedded string or message which claimed to have negative size.",uY:"Complete your profile to help improve your experience",AF:"Composition of a bullet point and an error message to be displayed in the Error Guide pane. \u2022 is the unicode representation of a bullet point",qH:"Content for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to deselect their current Google Cloud Platform project. The selected project is used to determine the Earth subscription plan available to the user. Google Cloud Platform does not need to be translated.",Bh:"Content for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to leave their current Earth subscription plan.",Tc:"Content for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to remove their profile data stored in settings.",g3:"Content for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to switch their current Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project. The selected GCP project determines the selected Earth subscription plan.",ct:"Content for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to switch their current Google Cloud Platform project. The selected project determines the selected Earth subscription plan. Google Cloud Platform does not need to be translated.",Po:"Content of a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to create more designs like this design using the same inputs and replace their existing draft inputs for new build designs created previously. Building designs refers to creating a new building or structure.",M5:"Content of a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to create more designs like this design using the same inputs and replace their existing draft inputs for solar feasibility designs created previously. Sollar feasibility refers to the feasibility of installing solar panels on a building.",F_:"Content of a dialog that prompts the user to refresh the app in order to enable their Google Earth Professional Advanced subscription.",ra:"Content of a dialog that prompts the user to refresh the app in order to enable their new Earth subscription plan (either Professional or Professional Advanced).",QD:"Content text for a dialog asking if the user wants to delete the attribute for the current key or for all the keys. Features have key/value pairs which are referred as attributes. The user pressed a delete button next to an attribute and the dialog is offering to suppress just that attribute or remove the key in the list of keys, which has the effect of removing all the attributes with this key in the document.",Pk:"Copy operation failed. The document does not allow copying.",wI:"Copyright legalese shown in the About dialog.",f3:"Couldn't request access. Please try again later.",TO:"Create a new design to turn strategies on to reduce your environmental impact.",t4:"Create a new file you can save in your browser",ga:"Create a new file you can save on your device",ui:"Create a new map or add your site to an existing one.",TG:"Create a new site study or add your site to an existing one. Only your site selection and Google data layers will appear in your site study. Any imported data layers will not be visible.",jf:"Create shareable maps, import files, and analyze data in Drive",sw:"DATA_LAYER_FEATURE_RESTYLING_IN_MIRTH_ENABLED",dH:"Data is not available for the current map view.\nPan or zoom to a different area.",nf:"Data layer features in the Professional Advanced plan. This is shown in a bulleted list of feature in the welcome dialog.",R9:"Data layer features in the Professional plan. This is shown in a bulleted list of feature in the welcome dialog.",V7:"Data layers cannot be added to projects in a Shared Drive. Please move your project in Google Drive.",aH:"Default display name for a custom unit mix type in the edit unit mix dialog. Unit mix refers to the mix of units that a building is made up of, e.g. 1-Bedroom, 2-Bedroom, etc.",iL:"Default option of the label style size selector.",sA:"Define your area of interest to get started.",Nd:"Define your area of interest to get started. You can create a classification layer for an area up to ",bh:"Define your target gross floor area across the whole site or for each parcel.",pU:"Description displayed to user to allow them to clear the search history on the device.",sc:"Description for a panel that allows the user to filter data layers by the area of the selected features.",To:"Description for a settings action that determines where the user will land when loading Earth.",m_:"Description for a tab that allows the user to filter data layers by the area of the selected features.",fa:"Description for the basement parking toggle in the parking tab of the generate designs workflow. Explains what will occur when the toggle is enabled.",gk:"Description for the step in the design inputs panel where the user is configuring sustainability strategies for NewBuild designs.",_K:"Description for the surface parking toggle in the user inputs panel that explains what will occur when the toggle is enabled.",js:'Description of the "Clean" Map Style, in which all base layer feature categories (e.g. roads, borders, names) have been hidden. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=55783',oY:'Description of the "Custom" Map Style, in which the selection of visible base layer feature categories (e.g. roads, borders, names) can be made by the user. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=55785',ic:'Description of the "Everything" Map Style, in which all possible base layer feature categories (e.g. roads, borders, names) are visible. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=55787',vr:'Description of the "Exploration" Map Style, in which we show a particular set of base layer feature categories (specifically roads, borders and names) that we consider well-suited for exploring the map, while hiding some other categories (e.g. POIs) to minimize clutter. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=55789',Lt:"Description of the Add Building Types dialog, explaining that the building templates the user selects will generate buildings that vary in size and configuration based on their specifications.",wD:"Description of the Buildings step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",dq:"Description of the Program step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. Gross floor area refers to the total area of a building's interior. The site is the area of land which may be developed and have buildings constructed on it, and it may consist of multiple parcels.",xZ:"Description of the Satellite Basemap Style.",j4:"Description of the Solar Financial step of the user inputs panel.",Tn:"Description text in the parking tab of the user inputs panel for generating designs. Describes what this collection of inputs are used for.",tc:"Design details solar financials summary table column header for lease and Price Pack Architecture (PPA) strategy related financial metrics. PPA is a common industry term for Price Pack Architecture and should not be translated",ca:"Design details solar financials summary table column header for purchase and loan related financial metrics.",Rt:"Design details table column header for a parking metrics table representing the gross area of a design that is allocated for parking.",p8:"Design details table column header for a parking metrics table representing the number of parking spaces for a design.",R3:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the amount of gross floor area allocated for a particular use, like residential or commercial, relative to the total gross floor area of the site. 'GFA' should not be translated.",ff:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the amount of net internal area (NIA). NIA is the amount of usable area.  'NIA' should not be translated.",BA:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the gross floor area (GFA) of a particular use type or total across the site. 'GFA' should not be translated.",Vc:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the number of entities, like parking spots or apartment units in a site.",SB:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the number of parking facilities for a design.",NM:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the percentage of space that cannot be used.",JE:"Design details table column header for a program metrics table representing the use types (e.g. residential, commercial, community, etc.) of a particular use type or total across the site.",A9:"Design details table column header for a sustainability metrics table representing sources of carbon emission mitigations (e.g. car usage, solar production, embodied carbon, etc).",Hf:"Design details table column header for a sustainability metrics table representing the emissions reduction that will result from the sustainability strategies selected for a design in a 10 year period.",CP:"Design details table column header for a sustainability metrics table representing the sustainability strategy applied to a design.",RN:"Design details table column header for a sustainability metrics table representing the total ten year carbon emissions of a design.",IJ:"Design details table column header for a unit type metrics table representing the average size (e.g. area) of a particular unit type. Example unit types include studio apartments, 2 bedroom apartments, etc",Ri:"Design details table column header for a unit type metrics table representing the number of building units for a particular unit type. Example unit types include studio apartments, 2 bedroom apartments, etc.",x4:"Design details table column header for a unit type metrics table representing the percentage of total building units for a particular unit type. Example unit types include studio apartments, 2 bedroom apartments, etc.",x7:"Design details table column header for a unit type metrics table representing the unit type. Example unit types include studio apartments, 2 bedroom apartments, etc.",b_:"Design details table row header a program metrics table representing the total gross floor area allocated for the entire site.",o0:"Design details table title for all tables that are in the financials section for a solar design.",uF:"Design details table title for all tables that are in the program section (e.g. program summary table, by parcel, design stats, etc).",_V:"Design details table title for all tables that are in the sustainability section (e.g. emissions summary table).",Ig:"Design details table title for the summary table in the sustainability section (e.g. emissions summary table).",bR:"Design generation is in Experimental. You've exceeded the maximum site size.",aD:"Design generation is temporarily unavailable.",v5:"Detailed text for the confirmation dialog.",B6:"Details about selecting a Google Cloud Platform project for billing in Google Earth. GCP refers to Google Cloud Platform and does not need to be translated.",TB:"Dialog message for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to copy a project. The message should be worded as a question which can be answered with 'OK' or 'Cancel'",ir:"Dialog message for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to create a new cloud project. The message should be worded as a question which can be answered with 'OK' or 'Cancel'",tH:"Dialog message for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to import a file. The message should be worded as a question which can be answered with 'OK' or 'Cancel'",xp:"Dialog message for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to import a project. The message should be worded as a question which can be answered with 'OK' or 'Cancel'",fg:"Dialog message for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to show the list of cloud projects. The message should be worded as a question which can be answered with 'OK' or 'Cancel'",Hz:"Dialog text shown when the user tries to save their changes to a project, but has not selected any projects to save.",qx:"Dialog title for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to copy a project.",Ol:"Dialog title for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to create a new cloud project.",VD:"Dialog title for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to import a file.",eO:"Dialog title for inviting user to sign in to Google Drive in order to import a project.",Jg:"Disable Historical Imagery to enable this layer",uz:"Discard your last saved site and inputs and start over with a new site.",zx:"Disclaimer shown at the top of a balloon containing HTML content, informing the user that the content of the balloon is controlled by the author of the project and that they should not enter passwords or other personal information.  This is important because the HTML might contain scripts, forms, text entry fields, or other content that mimics a sign-in page, which could be used in a phishing attack or an attempt at identity theft.",Pu:"Disclaimer text shown in an Alert Dialog when the user clicks the feedback button in the Earth AI Assistant chat message. It informs the user that their query will be included in the feedback data, and will be associated with their email address. In the UI, the a Learn More link is shown after this text.",QX:"Discover new features and easily access all your data and projects in one place",LL:"Display name for the mechnical building use type. This refers to the space within a building that is used for mechanical equipment, such as air conditioning, ventilation, or heating units.",pZ:"Display name for the parking building use type. This refers to the space within a building that is used for parking spaces (e.g. basement parking lots).",ML:"Display name for the residential building use type. This refers to the space within a building that is used for residential units.",l8:"Do you want to only delete the attribute from this feature or do you want to remove this attribute key across all the features in this document?",iV:"Don\u2019t worry, any previous work on this screen will be saved.",iH:"Draw a polygon to generate a contour layer.",aB:"Draw a polygon to generate a cut and fill layer.",DA:"Draw a polygon to generate a slope layer.",kM:"Draw a polygon to generate an aspect layer.",O0:"During Experimental phase, imports to data layers limited to one file at a time.",Ts:"EARTH_MATE_GOOGLE_ONE_STANDARD_BANNER_ENABLED",gu:"EARTH_MATE_OVERHEAD_IMAGERY_SEARCH_ENABLED",Y1:"EARTH_WITH_GEMINI_PROMOTIONAL_MODAL_ENABLED",it:"ERROR_TYPE_MOVE_FEATURES_BETWEEN_DOCUMENTS_FAILED",gr:"ERROR_TYPE_PASTE_FAILED_FEATURE_COUNT_LIMIT_REACHED",HN:"ERROR_TYPE_PASTE_FAILED_USER_NOT_SIGNED_IN",Y_:"Edit styling for multiple features at once, without extra clicks",M8:"Elevation estimate label for a text field above the elevation statistics. Elevation is defined as the difference in meters or feet between the user's current location and the location of the point on the globe.",rf:"Emission reduction compared to total ten year or lifetime emission for this design without strategies applied",Pr:"Empty text indicating the user should select a Residential or Hotel use type to get additional options for advanced use type settings.",dR:"End animation for showing a place from search or knowledge card.",c3:"Energy (other renewable; not solar or wind)",gl:"Enter desired gross area for each parking spot, including the size of the spot itself and circulation space.",Cg:"Error generating description, refresh to try again",TC:"Error handler must accept one Object or one Object and a StackTrace as arguments, and return a value of the returned future's type",O:"Error message displayed in the Error Guide pane following a conversion error during a file import.",xL:"Error message displayed in the Error Guide pane following an error during a file import.",W7:"Error message displayed in the Error Guide pane following an unsupported file type error during a file import.",sB:"Error message displayed in the Error Guide pane when the dataset is empty after a file import.",eI:"Error message displayed in the bullet point list in the Error Guide pane following a conversion error during a file import.",HT:"Error message displayed in the full error log from a failed file import.",HP:"Error message indicating that the current knowledge card failed to load, likely due to a network connectivity issue.",AV:"Error message informing the user that the copy operation failed because one or all of the affected features do not allow copying.",GV:"Error message informing the user that the copy operation failed because the document does not allow copying.",rG:"Error message informing the user that the project name cannot be empty.",id:"Error message informing users that copying a project has timed out.",Ss:"Error message notifying the user that an error occurred during image generation.",K_:"Error message show in a toast when the user selects file to import whose type is not supported.",Xa:"Error message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window if permission problems occurred during this request.",Oa:"Error message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window if the request timed out.",q7:"Error message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window if the request was rejected due to too many requests being sent too quickly.",cl:"Error message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window if the user has reached their daily query limit.",XI:"Error message shown to the user when the total percentage of all unit mix values is not 100%.",IE:"Error message shown to user when they try to add a YouTube video that has already been added to a feature.",nU:"Error message shown when a user tries to request access to a project, but the request fails.",E_:"Error message shown when the Earth app fails to start properly because a problem occurred when trying to obtain values needed for app startup from a configuration file.",PK:"Error message shown when the mobile app fails to fetch configuration values needed at startup due to auth errors. Ask users to clear their app data and reload.",AZ:"Error message shown when the user has submitted a set of inputs to generate designs, but an error occurred during the generation process.",eG:"Error message shown when the web app fails to fetch configuration values needed at startup due to auth errors. Ask users to clear the cookies from the Earth website and reload.",Xo:"Error text shown when user enters an invalid URL.",ri:"Error text under a text-input field that says the input hexadecimal color is not long enough.",IW:"Error: WebGL is not supported on your browser",gZ:"Estimate the volume of earth to excavate (cut) and add (fill) to create a flat site for an area of interest up to ",a5:"Estimate the volume of earth to excavate (cut) and add (fill) to create a flat site for an area of interest, minimizing the net volume.",hV:"Estimates vary with map view resolution and are refined once you finish drawing. Measurements are inferred based on the latest data and are not survey-grade.",Je:"Excess: Sell extra solar energy after used on site",WQ:"Explanation of why a feature is restricted from being exported to a KML file.",na:"Explanatory text for a dialog that asks the user if they want to request access to the owner of a project.",Xt:"Explanatory text in a dialog notifying the user that the Timelapse feature is now available from the Basemap Settings menu.",Mu:"Explanatory text in a dialog notifying the user that the Voyager feature has moved outside of the Earth app",Ce:"Explore Google's catalog of historical imagery of the planet.",xa:"Explore points of interest and natural features, plus infrastructure data in the United States",ba:"Explore recommended designs, make changes, and visualize them on a map",KH:"External image has reached the maximum fetch limit",SA:"Extra large option in the size selector for points and labels in a layer.",zZ:"Extra large option of the label style size selector.",Fe:"Failed to communicate with the backend server.",Hg:"Failed to fetch startup values. Please retry or reload the app.",_N:"Failed to fetch startup values. Please try clearing app data and reload.",ch:"Failed to fetch startup values. Please try clearing cookies from this site and reload the page.",GQ:"Failed to register and synchronize mendel package ",NH:"Feature name appended with an accessibility label describing a 3D model feature.",xX:"Filter a layer based on its relationship to an area.",mI:"Find and manage all your projects in Google Earth.",Qt:"Floor type refers to the type of use for a floor, such as residential, commercial, or industrial.",pB:"For a personalized experience and more relevant feature updates, share some info about how you use Earth.",oW:"Freshwater (e.g. rivers, estuaries, groundwater)",E6:"GCP_STANDARD_USER_PROMOTION_BANNER_ENABLED",qk:"Generate 100 building and solar designs per month, up to 5 acres",Xp:"Generate a slope layer with a resolution of ",MM:"Generate an aspect layer with a resolution of ",cJ:"Generate the best options for your real estate development, such as building designs and solar for sites larger than 0.5 acres.",VF:"Generic error message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window.",nz:"GeoJSON and JSON files cannot yet be imported as map features.",KF:"GeoJSON, JSON, and Shapefile (ZIP) files cannot be imported as map features.",WL:"Get detailed performance metrics and renderings of your designs to optimize for quality of life. Larger sites will take 5-15 minutes to generate.",vH:"Get insights about your project by selecting features or importing KML data",Kj:"Give your untitled map a name before it's shared",UF:"Give your untitled site study a name before it's shared",Jm:"Go to View > Start slideshow to view in presentation mode.",c_:"Google Drive must be installed, enabled and up to date to import Earth projects",tj:"Google Earth shows zoning requirements for your parcel based on local data.",si:"HIGHER_CAPABILITY_AVAILABLE_VIA_OTHER_LICENSE",MO:"HIGHER_CAPABILITY_AVAILABLE_VIA_PLAN_UPGRADE",e6:"HOMESCREEN_PROJECT_LIST_FILTERING_SERVER_SIDE_ENABLED",hM:"Header for a UI that lets the user drop placemarks (points with an associated icon) on the map.",ib:"Header for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to deselect their current Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project. GCP does not need to be translated.",c2:"Header for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to leave their current Earth subscription plan.",K4:"Header for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to remove their profile data stored in settings.",mn:"Header for a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to switch their current Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project. The selected GCP project determines the selected Earth subscription plan. GCP does not need to be translated.",_Q:"Header for a dropdown section of the building editor that allows the user to edit advanced settings of a buildings floor group. You can edit the loss factor of the floor group. Loss factor represents the percentage of space that cannot be used.",H_:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the average height of buildings in a design.",fR:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the number of buildings in a design.",Md:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the percentage of ground parcel area covered by buildings for a design.",IZ:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the percentage of street wall filled with buildings for a design.",Wb:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the shortest building height in a design.",IS:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the tallest building height in a design.",Dt:"Header for a row in the design stats metrics table in the design details panel, representing the total facade area of all buildings in a design.",Fj:"Header for a row in the new build emissions summary metrics table in the design details panel, representing the distance travelled by automobiles. The number of automobiles is estimated from parking lots included in the design.",kF:"Header for a row in the solar financials metrics table in the design details panel, representing the net present value of a solar design. The net present value is a financial metric that compares expected cashflow to initial investment to assess the value of a project.",eu:"Header for a row in the solar financials table in the design details panel, representing the payback period for a solar design. This represents the number of years it will take to break even on the investment for solar panels.",CH:"Header for a section of the building editor that allows the user to edit the floor groups of a building. You can edit the configuration of each floor group, such as the number of floors, the height of the floor, and the use type of the floor. Stacking plan refers to the order in which the floors are built which is also editable.",WA:"Header for a section that allows the user to configure how the site analysis layer is created. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",WR:"Header for a section that allows the user to select their Google Cloud Platform project for billing in Google Earth.",Ic:"Header for a section that allows the user to select their Google Cloud Platform project.",Bb:"Header for a section that contains billing plan details in Google Earth.",o1:"Header for a section where users are instructed to define classes and add sample points for a classification layer.",PA:"Header for a section where users can define and edit classification classes.",pQ:"Header for a set of basement floor groups within a dialog to edit a building's configuration.",Rk:"Header for a set of fields that allows the user to specify the number of floors in a building.",ih:"Header for a set of floor groups that share a common building configuration that alters the shape of the floor groups using a bar type geometry operation. An operation is a mathematical geometry operation applied to the building. A bar shaped floor is a floor that is rectangular and ensures a uniform lease depth. A bar geometry op is where one edge of the origin polygon is offset a specific distance.",E8:"Header for a set of floor groups that share a common building configuration that alters the shape of the floor groups using a floating type geometry operation. An operation is a mathematical geometry operation applied to the building. A floating operation is specifying a new geometry shape for the floor group. ",Px:"Header for a set of floor groups that share a common building configuration that alters the shape of the floor groups using a setback type geometry operation. An operation is a mathematical geometry operation applied to the building. A setback operation is shaving off a set distance along one of the facades of a building.",M2:"Header for a set of floor groups that share a common building configuration that alters the shape of the floor groups using a simplify type geometry operation. An operation is a mathematical geometry operation applied to the building. A simplify operation is where the building is simplified to a simpler shape.",Pp:"Header for a set of floor groups that share a common building configuration that alters the shape of the floor groups using a wrap type geometry operation. An operation is a mathematical geometry operation applied to the building. A wrap operation is where a use type of a building wraps around a different internal use type of floor. A use type describes the floors intended usage such as being used for residential, ofice, or retail space.",Dr:"Header for a sheet or dialog that asks the user to specify where to add a data layer, whether to a new Drive project or a local KML file or a pre-existing project or file",ez:"Header for a sheet or dialog that asks the user to specify where to save a feature, whether to a new Drive project or a local KML file or a pre-existing project or file",Xd:"Header for a sheet or dialog that asks the user to specify where to start design generation, whether to a new Drive project or a pre-existing project.",r0:"Header for a tab that allows the user to filter data layers by the area of the selected features.",Tz:"Header for a table row showing the twenty five year savings for a solar project.",My:"Header for a table row showing the upfront cost of solar panels after incentives (e.g. national and state tax credits, rebates, cash) have been applied.",WZ:"Header for an info card that is shown when a user is in polygon selection mode but there are no polygons in the current project.",Tt:"Header for the entrypoint to the area filter tool in the Filter tab of the Data Layer Details panel.",qF:"Header for the garage parking table row for the parking metrics table in the design details panel.",h5:"Header for the section of the Generate Designs Site tab view that shows the zoning information for each parcel. Zoning requirements refers to the rules and regulations that govern the use of land and buildings in a particular area.",S5:"Header for the surface parking table row for the parking metrics table in the design details panel.",l5:"Header label for a left hand panel UI that shows the details of a project.",dg:"Header label for a section of UI that lists the user's Earth projects stored locally on this device (i.e. phone memory card, or computer hard drive).",ld:"Header label for app bar that asks the user if they want to request access to the owner of a project.",kG:"Header label for column in for use type constraints on site development program targets.",NT:"Header of a card inviting the user to interact with the Data Catalog in Google Earth.",qf:"Header of a category showing keyboard shortcuts related to navigation on the 3D map (pan, tilt, zoom, etc).",de:"Header of a section that allows the user to set attributes to a feature.",G4:'Header of a section that allows the user to set the viewpoint from which a feature on the map is viewed when you fly to it. The section lets the user specify the view by manually entering the latitude, longitude, altitude, heading, range, and tilt (as opposed to just positioning the camera somewhere and clicking "Snapshot current view", which is the usual method).',Fk:"Header text displayed in the Error Guide pane following a conversion error during a file import.",zF:"Header to promote the Earth AI assistant button when it is first introduced to the user.",tw:"Header to promote the create more button. This prompts users to change the inputs or information that they have entered to create a previous building development or solar panel design so that they can create more designs like this one.",er:"Heading for a banner shown to users who have a Google One plan describing the added benefits when using Earth Mate, when there is no specific plan name to mention.",bP:"Heading for a section that asks the user to optionally opt-in to receiving marketing communications.",Sb:"Heading for an info section of the design generation panel that describes the first step in using the design generation tool.",MP:"Heading for an info section of the design generation panel that describes the second step in using the design generation tool.",Zb:"Heading for an info section of the design generation panel that describes the third step in using the design generation tool.",L9:"Heading must be UTF-8. Ensure the heading specifies UTF-8 encoding and try again.",Ut:"Help text for the aspect analysis view. Aspect is the direction that a slope faces. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",ac:"Help text for the contour analysis view. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",K8:"Help text for the cut and fill analysis view. Cut and fill analysis is a process that measures the volume of earth material that needs to be moved to create a level area of land.",cT:"Help text for the slope analysis view. Slope is the steepness of the terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",GI:"Helper text for the area selection tool for classification layers.",hd:"High contrast is enabled by your operating system",wA:"Historical Imagery mode temporarily disables 3D buildings for optimal viewing.",j:"Host platform returned null value for non-null return value.",M1:"How fast you will fly to search results and other places on the globe.",nu:"INDUSTRY_ARTIFICIAL_INTELLIGENCE_AND_MACHINE_LEARNING",ik:"INDUSTRY_BUSINESS_AND_PROFESSIONAL_SERVICES",WJ:"INDUSTRY_ELECTRICAL_GRID_UTILITIES_OPERATIONS",ey:"INDUSTRY_FLEET_MANAGEMENT_AND_GPS_TRACKING",Mz:"INDUSTRY_INDUSTRIAL_GOODS_AND_MANUFACTURING",EC:"INDUSTRY_LAND_AND_COASTAL_ECOSYSTEMS_MANAGEMENT_AND_CONSERVATION",im:"INDUSTRY_OCEANS_ECOSYSTEMS_AND_CONSERVATION",gx:"INDUSTRY_SCIENTIFIC_RESEARCH_AND_DEVELOPMENT",RH:"INDUSTRY_SELECTOR_ALWAYS_SHOW_CTA_ENABLED",LD:"INDUSTRY_UTILITIES_PLANNING_OR_OPERATIONS",JO:"If enabled, drawing tools will add content at the center of the window instead of at the mouse or touch location.",Hl:"If you continue, any existing inputs you have for building designs will be discarded.",p2:"If you continue, any existing inputs you have for solar feasibility designs will be discarded.",jQ:"If your Google Earth plan has been upgraded, click refresh below to enable the new features and see them in your settings.",Bq:"If your parcel spans multiple zones, the displayed requirements will be based on the largest zone within that parcel.",y7:"Impact numbers are calculated by comparing this design to a baseline that doesn't use any sustainability strategies.",RX:"Import complete with errors - see error details",V1:"Import data like addresses and place names to visualize and analyze on a map",il:"Import error: the selected file type is not supported",Py:"Import error: unable to write to the server",EE:"Import failed due to excessive address geocoding errors. Please review and correct the addresses in your file before re-importing.",gb:"Import failed due to excessive address geocoding errors. The maximum number of geocoding errors is ",jL:"Import failed due to excessive geometry errors. Please verify the assigned geometry and re-import the file.",fG:"Import failed due to excessive geometry errors. Please verify the assigned geometry and re-import the file. The maximum number of geometry errors is ",ok:"Import failed. Adding all features from the file would exceed the map's limit. Currently, only ",U7:"Import failed. Adding all features from the file would exceed the map's limit. Currently, only one feature in the file can be imported without exceeding the limit.",D1:"Import failed. Your file exceeded the feature limit (",Vp:"Import failed: Map has reached its maximum feature limit of ",QP:"Import failed: Map has reached its maximum feature limit.",uo:"In order to access your paid plan, you must use the GCP project associated with it.",ph:"In some locations, you can explore historical imagery from multiple dates.",je:"Included with Professional and Professional Advanced plans",yB:"Incorrect encoding. Ensure the file is UTF-8 encoded and try again.",um:"Increases the contrast for better visibility",Ek:"Information text in the copy document dialog that informs the user that the designs will not be copied to the new project.",hZ:"Informational label that signals to the user that there are at the moment unsaved changes in the editor UI.",yr:"Informational text to describe the behavior for a checkbox that will signal whether or not design generation should estimate the energy usage of the site or use the user's provided values. When enabled, it will use the user's provided values.",tY:"Informative text shown to the user to tell them that they have no Earth projects.",bp:"Input ended with incomplete encoded byte.",zN:"Input label for the front yard setback zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site (e.g. a land area location) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",Qo:"Input label for the maximum building coverage ratio zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site (e.g. a land area location) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",NR:"Input label for the maximum floor area ratio zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site (e.g. a land area location) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",yJ:"Input label for the maximum height  zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site (e.g. a land area location) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",_z:"Input label for the minimum open space ratio zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site (e.g. a land area location) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",wg:"Input label for the number of parking spots in the parking tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",GZ:"Input label for the side yard setback zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site (e.g. a land area location) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",Qz:"Input label in the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to set an area for parking spots (e.g. a parking spot is 10 sq m)",_g:"Input your criteria, including use type and building mix",d3:"Instructional text for adding classification classes and sample points in the classification layer editor.",MS:"Instructional text to describe the cut and fill analysis tool. Cut and fill analysis is a process that measures the volume of earth material that needs to be moved to create a level area of land.",AR:"Instructions for on-demand analysis and evaluation tools that indicates a user can begin drawing a polygon on the map to begin analysis.",rm:"Instructions in an info section of the design generation panel that explains the user's first step when using the design generation tool.",Uf:"Instructions in an info section of the design generation panel that explains the user's second step when using the design generation tool.",Pm:"Instructions in an info section of the design generation panel that explains the user's third step when using the design generation tool.",qe:"IntlOneGoogleLocalizations_signedInAsAccount",kr:"IntlOneGoogleLocalizations_unnamedAccount",nG:"Invalid XML heading. Correct the file's heading and try again.",AL:"Invalid file type. Please import a KML or KMZ file.",q0:"Invalid file type. Please import a KML, KMZ, or GeoJSON file.",dO:"KML export is not available for this document",DR:"KML import, historical satellite imagery and Street View & more",aW:"Keep this app open, or import progress will be lost",C7:"Keep this tab open, or import progress will be lost",_L:"Knowledge card failed to load.  You may be offline.",rt:"LAYER_OUTPUT_DISABLED_IN_PROGRESS_LRO_IMPORT",qW:"LAYER_OUTPUT_DISABLED_VALIDATION_FAILED_NOT_OWNER",Nk:"LAYER_OUTPUT_DISABLED_VALIDATION_FAILED_SHARED_DRIVE",c5:"LAYER_OUTPUT_DISABLED_VALIDATION_FAILED_UNKNOWN",_i:"Label (or hint text) of a text field where the user can enter the name for a new document.",Rq:"Label any use types defined by users or not otherwise specified.",i7:"Label button to refresh the current web page.",eV:"Label describing a keyboard shortcut (a series of keypresses) that will produce a specific action when performed.",QT:"Label describing a keyboard shortcut (a series of keypresses) that will produce a specific action when performed.  This needs to fit on a single line along with the shortcut text, so please keep it as short as possible.",uj:"Label describing an expandable tile that contains quick actions.",qX:"Label for a button allowing the user to share a link with other users.",AH:"Label for a button allowing the user to share a screenshot of their current Earth view.",d:"Label for a button in the menu panel that opens the settings dialog.",T:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to cancel the actions they have just performed.",V:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to close the view or panel that is currently being shown.",Lv:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to remove the view or panel that is currently being shown.",xd:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to restart the presentation of a project from the beginning.",T0:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to resume the currently paused project in Present mode.",l:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to save the changes they have just performed.",fj:"Label for a button indicating that the user wishes to toggle the table of contents for a project in Present mode.",ig:"Label for a button or menu item which copies the current feature's style information -- color, icon, line width, etc. The copy is internal to Earth and does not use the system clipboard; it could alternately be thought of as 'remember for later use'.",gs:"Label for a button or menu item which copies the current line's style information -- color, line width, etc.  The copy is internal to Earth and does not use the system clipboard; it could alternately be thought of as 'remember for later use'.",lF:"Label for a button or menu item which copies the current point's style information -- color, icon, etc.  The copy is internal to Earth and does not use the system clipboard; it could alternately be thought of as 'remember for later use'.",MT:"Label for a button or menu item which copies the current polygon's style information -- color, line width, fill color, etc.  The copy is internal to Earth and does not use the system clipboard; it could alternately be thought of as 'remember for later use'.",Ja:"Label for a button or menu item which pastes style information into the current feature -- color, icon, line width, etc. The paste is not from the system clipboard, but from a style that the user previously 'copied' within the Earth application.",tU:"Label for a button or menu item which pastes style information into the current line feature -- color, line width, etc.  The paste is not from the system clipboard, but from a style that the user previously 'copied' within the Earth application.",ZF:"Label for a button or menu item which pastes style information into the current point feature -- color, icon, etc.  The paste is not from the system clipboard, but from a style that the user previously 'copied' within the Earth application.",zm:"Label for a button or menu item which pastes style information into the current polygon feature -- color, line width, fill color, etc.  The paste is not from the system clipboard, but from a style that the user previously 'copied' within the Earth application.",i:"Label for a button or menu item which resets the style information of the current feature to default values -- color, icon, line width, etc.",g5:"Label for a button that adds a description to a feature. Shown together with a + sign",ms:"Label for a button that adds an attribute to a feature. Shown together with a + sign",FL:"Label for a button that adds an image or video to a feature. Shown together with a + sign",h:"Label for a button that allows the user to confirm that they are finished with their current action.",FZ:"Label for a button that allows the user to downgrade to the Professional plan.",tL:"Label for a button that allows the user to downgrade to the Standard plan.",I9:"Label for a button that allows the user to leave the current Earth subscription plan.",Vm:"Label for a button that allows the user to open the details panel which displays all metrics and details for the selected single design.",vS:"Label for a button that allows the user to open the home screen which displays all projects owned by that user.",cO:"Label for a button that allows the user to report a legal issue (Content relating to country/region-specific laws, such as privacy or intellectual property laws).",A0:"Label for a button that allows the user to report abusive content.",A8:"Label for a button that allows the user to report inappropriate content.",j9:"Label for a button that allows the user to try the Professional plans for free as part of an experimental release.",l3:"Label for a button that applies the filter for data layers by the area of the selected features.",yv:"Label for a button that causes the model being edited to be moved to the lat/lon position the camera is currently looking at.",z4:"Label for a button that clears an area filter that has been applied to a data layer.",ee:"Label for a button that closes the Earth AI assistant chat window.",kL:"Label for a button that collapses an imagery grid to show fewer images.",Nq:"Label for a button that enters into map measuring mode.",oi:"Label for a button that is disabled because it is the currently subscribed Earth subscription plan.",gQ:"Label for a button that lets the user choose a background color for the current feature's info box.",dl:"Label for a button that opens a dialog to upgrade the user's storage plan.",EF:"Label for a button that opens a link to a page to manager the users in the current Earth subscription plan.",t:"Label for a button that opens a link with all Earth subscription plans.",F4:"Label for a button that opens the Earth Mate side panel.",mz:"Label for a button that will hide the timeline of Street View imagery and show the latest imagery.",Za:"Label for a button that will show the dates of the timeline of Street View imagery.",nd:'Label for a button that, when clicked, will allow the user to start presenting the feature or project they\'re currently viewing in presentation mode. "Present" here is a verb, and has the sense of a slide deck.',aK:"Label for a button to add a feature to a project.",d5:"Label for a button to add a new classifier class in the classification layer editor.",g9:"Label for a button to enable real estate and clean energy development tools.",ZE:"Label for a button to reload a knowledge card, typically only needed when there is a network connectivity issue.",fY:"Label for a button to reload the web page.",_9:"Label for a button to report a bug or issue encountered while loading details for a selected layer feature.",RP:"Label for a button toggle that allows users to filter the view to see a list of designs that were starred by the user.",Dv:"Label for a checkbox in the UI for copying a project. When checked, the copy of the project will be shared with the same people as the original project.",cp:"Label for a context menu item on a message (prompt) sent to the Earth AI assistant. This action copies the message into the prompt field, allowing the user to edit the prompt before submitting it. This is useful for making small modifications to an already submitted prompt.",Hu:"Label for a context menu item on a message (prompt) sent to the Earth AI assistant. This action resends the prompt, which is useful for retrying due to an error or failure.",r4:"Label for a count of features of a given type in a project, which allows users to understand the information items they see in the insepector panel. The count is shown when users select multiple features of different types and the information item is shown for the same feature type.",Uu:"Label for a design group that has failed to generate.",XM:"Label for a dialog that asks the user if they want to request access to the owner of project they can't see",gf:"Label for a drawn polygon. This is shown to indicate that the area was drawn by the user.",bd:"Label for a dropdown for selecting a color ramp to style a layer by. A color ramp is a thematic set of colors representing sequential values or different categories of values.",is:"Label for a dropdown menu that allows the user to select a year for a classification layer.",L4:"Label for a dropdown that allows the user to select a polygon from their project to use in some operation.",Cw:"Label for a dropdown widget that displays a currently selected icon and opens a popup picker panel that allows the user to select an icon.",zW:"Label for a dropdown widget that displays the currently selected color and opens a popup picker panel that allows the user to select a color.",jS:'Label for a fact item containing the approximate centroid of the selected points.  "Centroid" is a geospatial term referring to the "center of mass" of the points on the surface of the Earth',Yv:"Label for a fact item containing the approximate distance between two features. Distance refers to the geodesic distance between the two locations over the surface of the Earth, ignoring the altitude of those two locations and any terrain between those locations.",YQ:"Label for a fact item containing the number of features that are contained within a particular folder or document.",Ge:"Label for a field that allows the user to specify the height of a floor within a floor group in a building.",_Y:"Label for a field that allows the user to specify the maximum number of floors in a floor group in a building.",Pw:"Label for a field that allows the user to specify the minimum number of floors in a floor group in a building.",qC:"Label for a icon button that takes the user from the design viewer to the list of all their projects in the left hand panel.",f_:"Label for a keyboard shortcut that hides or shows the menu bar at the top of the view.",G:"Label for a link that brings users to a page to report problematic images.",_M:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of a distance calculation using a particular unit of measure.",rp:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of a distance calculation using a particular unit of measure. A smoot is an obscure unit of measurement whose name is derived from the name of a person, Oliver R. Smoot. It can therefore generally be transliterated directly into your language's alphabet or syllabary.",Xb:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of a distance calculation using a particular unit of measure. This refers specifically to the imperial yard, which is three feet.",IF:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of a slope calculation using degrees as the unit of measure.",YT:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of a slope calculation using percent as the unit of measure.",bj:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of an area calculation using a particular unit of measure.",sM:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to display the results of an area calculation using a particular unit of measure. This refers specifically to the imperial yard, which is three feet.",Mo:"Label for a menu item allowing the user to open the settings dialog and edit their settings for units of measurement.",pm:"Label for a menu item that hides the highlighted streets where users can enter streetview from.",H9:"Label for a menu item that hides the menu bar at the top of the view.",P:"Label for a menu item that lets a user permanently delete a Google Earth project.",w6:"Label for a menu item that shows information about the currently selected latitude and longitude on the globe.",Sa:"Label for a menu item that shows the highlighted streets where users can enter streetview from.",CG:"Label for a menu option that lets users create a full screen slide in their project that is not tied to a geographical feature or location.",oe:"Label for a menu option that lets users create a tile overlay showing raster data in their project.",Ha:"Label for a menu that allows the user to select a country or region.",a_:"Label for a menu that allows users to change the option for sorting a list of Built Environment designs.",zG:"Label for a navigation item that brings the user to a list of all of their Google Earth projects",CR:"Label for a panel that shows projects created or opened by the user.",q9:"Label for a popup button for choosing a key when configuring key/value pairs associated with a feature.",ek:"Label for a popup button for choosing the type (string, number, ...) for a value when configuring key/value pairs associated with a feature.",kP:"Label for a popup menu that allows the user to change their basemap styles.",ZK:"Label for a popup menu that lets the user choose the opacity percentage for the fill of a polygon",ve:"Label for a popup menu that lets the user choose the pixel width for the border of a polygon",ty:"Label for a progress indicator that shows the user's storage usage is full.",a4:"Label for a progress indicator that shows the user's storage usage.",LO:"Label for a section that lets users modify the coverage (aka extents, aka bounding box) of a tile overlay, which defines on what region of the globe the tiles are located.  The values being set here are measured in degrees latitude or longitude.",Ld:"Label for a section that shows built-in basemap styles, like 3D (Satellite), 2D (Roadmap), etc.",A3:"Label for a section that shows built-in customizable basemap details, like like borders, roads, labels, photos, etc.",dC:"Label for a selection choice for DD:MM.mmm latitude/longitude formatting, with degrees and decimal minutes. E.g. [46\xb034.354'].",Ve:"Label for a selection choice for DD:MM:SS latitude/longitude formatting. E.g. [46\xb034'21\"].",QN:"Label for a selection choice for decimal latitude/longitude formatting. E.g. [46.589234\xb0].",pp:"Label for a selection choice for imperial distance units.",io:"Label for a selection choice for metric distance units.",lD:"Label for a selection choice for the Explore view as the default loading destination.",l_:"Label for a selection choice for the Homescreen as the default loading destination.",ho:"Label for a setting option in google earth that governs the overall fly animation speed for camera.",e9:"Label for a setting option that allow user to choose the type of animation to play for showing a place or region.",pK:"Label for a settings action that allows the user to update their response to the user profile survey.",y5:"Label for a settings action that clears Earth's data cache.",AY:"Label for a settings action that clears the list of allowed and blocked domains.",yR:"Label for a settings action that determines where the user will land when loading Earth.",q5:"Label for a settings action that removes previously filled out user profile data from Earth.",X3:"Label for a settings action that takes the user to Google's location system settings.",CK:"Label for a tab that lists the user's Earth projects in Google Drive. Located under an app bar with 'Your projects' title.",og:"Label for a tab that lists the user's Earth projects stored locally on this device (i.e. phone memory card, or computer hard drive). Located under an app bar with 'Your projects' title.",hG:"Label for a text button that takes the user back from viewing details of a single project to the list of all their projects.",Ih:"Label for a text button that will randomly select a place on the Earth.",dd:"Label for a text button used as a follow up action to the 'I'm feeling lucky' action to pick the next random location. Ideally should be a single, short word.",Lh:"Label for a text field allowing the user to change the title of a project",PB:"Label for a text field containing a Plus Code: https://maps.google.com/pluscodes/",Vl:"Label for a text field containing the altitude of a 3D model on the globe. This will be a number whose implied unit is meters.",ie:"Label for a text field containing the altitude of a point on the globe. This will be a number whose implied unit is meters.",iv:"Label for a text field containing the amount of a 3D model should be scaled in the X direction.",Lx:"Label for a text field containing the amount of a 3D model should be scaled in the Y direction.",Jo:"Label for a text field containing the amount of a 3D model should be scaled in the Z direction.",TP:"Label for a text field containing the amount of rotation associated with a 3D model.",Hh:"Label for a text field containing the distance the model should be moved in a eastern direction (with negative values moving west).",zM:"Label for a text field containing the distance the model should be moved in a northern direction (with negative values moving south).",ub:"Label for a text field containing the duration of an event, such as a tour or video. This will be a localized time stamp, which in English might appear as e.g. 12:34.",oq:"Label for a text field containing the elevation gain of a path on the globe. This will be a number, most often in feet or meters.",cU:"Label for a text field containing the elevation loss of a path on the globe. This will be a number, most often in feet or meters.",iA:"Label for a text field containing the elevation. This will be a number, most often in feet or meters. Elevation is defined as the height of a point above sea level.",b1:"Label for a text field containing the ground elevation for placemarks. This will be a number, most often in feet or meters. Ground elevation is defined as the height of a point above sea level.",rB:"Label for a text field containing the latitude of a 3D model on the globe. This will be a number between -90 and 90, whose implied unit is degrees.",OO:"Label for a text field containing the latitude of a point on the globe. This will be a number between -90 and 90, whose implied unit is degrees.",JU:"Label for a text field containing the latitude of the northern edge of an overlay on the globe. This will be a number between -90 and 90, whose implied unit is degrees.",Tu:"Label for a text field containing the latitude of the southern edge of an overlay on the globe. This will be a number between -90 and 90, whose implied unit is degrees.",vZ:"Label for a text field containing the length of a line string. This will be a number whose unit will be one of feet, miles, kilometers, etc.",R7:"Label for a text field containing the longitude of a 3D model on the globe. This will be a number between -180 and 180, whose implied unit is degrees.",kN:"Label for a text field containing the longitude of a point on the globe. This will be a number between -180 and 180, whose implied unit is degrees.",Rb:"Label for a text field containing the longitude of the eastern edge of an overlay on the globe. This will be a number between -180 and 180, whose implied unit is degrees.",sy:"Label for a text field containing the longitude of the western edge of an overlay on the globe. This will be a number between -180 and 180, whose implied unit is degrees.",X8:"Label for a text field containing the number of tax lots selected in site selection. A tax lot is a property recorded on the government tax map. The number is a non-negative value.",PM:"Label for a text field containing the perimeter of a polygon. This will be a number whose unit will be one of feet, miles, kilometers, etc.",nB:"Label for a text field containing the physical street address associated with a point on the globe.  This may or may not include city, country, postal code, etc.",qB:"Label for a text field that allows the user to enter a number that specifies the interval of a contour analysis layer. The interval is the distance between the elevation of the contour lines on the map.",Df:"Label for a text field that allows the user to enter a number that specifies the resolution of a slope or aspect analysis layer. The resolution is the pixel density of the output raster data.",T3:"Label for a text field that describes an area of a boundary on the globe. Only shown if the user has drawn a closed polygon.",DN:"Label for a text field that lets users edit the URL pattern used for a tile overlay.",xq:"Label for a text field that lets users edit the size (in pixels) of tiles that make up a tile overlay.",Ym:"Label for a text field where the user can enter a display name for their chosen classification class.",ax:"Label for a toggle button on the setting panel to enable or disable the fly animation. The fly animation is the animation that transitions the camera from the current view to the final view.",Tp:"Label for a toggle button that enables the Earth AI Assistant to use the satellite imagery search tool.",Lb:"Label for a toggle button to cloud animations in Google Earth.",eL:"Label for a toggle button to enable 3D buildings in Google Earth.",t7:"Label for a toggle button to enable 3D coverage layer in Google Earth.",Iu:"Label for a toggle button to enable recently updated satellite or aerial imagery layer in Google Earth.",Hv:"Label for a toggle button to enable the Historical Imagery feature.",Zk:"Label for a toggle button to gridlines in Google Earth.",Eb:"Label for a toggle that displays all reference projects on the globe. A reference project is a project the user wants to reference while working on a separate project.",yf:"Label for a toggle that, when checked, will display all reference projects on the globe. A reference project is a project the user wants to reference while working on a separate project.",Th:"Label for a user profile setting that describes how the user uses the Google Earth app.",OC:"Label for a user profile setting that describes the geographic countries or regions that the user's work focuses on.",ak:"Label for a user profile setting that describes the geographic scale of the work the user does.",QK:"Label for a user profile setting that describes which industries the user works in.",SE:"Label for a user provided name for a building use type. For example a building use type could be 'Residential' and a user could give it a custom name of 'My high density residential'.",No:"Label for an edit field for setting the value when configuring key/value pairs associated with a feature.",s8:"Label for an editor section that lets users edit the style of tile overlays, such as tile URL pattern and extents.",n_:"Label for an expandable section that contains additional settings for a path during bulk styling.",FI:"Label for an expandable section that contains additional settings for a placemark during bulk styling.",M6:"Label for an expandable section that contains additional settings for a polygon during bulk styling.",MZ:"Label for an expandable section that features additional settings.",Nb:"Label for an inkwell icon button that allows the user to open a panel that displays all of the built environment design contents for a project.",oa:"Label for button that opens a dialog allowing users to manage their reference projects. Reference projects are projects the user wants to remain visible while working on a separate project.",t5:"Label for describing the new build design metric showing the total area of the building.",yK:"Label for describing the type of design that generates new developments. Used as the name of a group of designs when viewing groups of designs by type.",Co:"Label for describing the type of design that generates solar panels. Used as the name of a group of designs when viewing groups of designs by type.",zd:"Label for expandable 'Placemark Placement' section of the property editor.",C9:"Label for field that allows the user to specify the corridor width of a floor group in a building. A corridor is a passage connecting parts of a building like a hallway.",rV:"Label for field that allows the user to specify the lease depth of a floor group in a building. Lease depth is the distance from the exterior facade to the core or corridor for this group of floors. Lease describes the actual rentable building area between the facade and the core.",wo:"Label for field that allows the user to specify the loss factor of a floor group in a building. Loss factor represents the percentage of space that cannot be used. This is the amount of lost space.",Ls:"Label for grouping a set of NewBuild designs by date. Each group name contains the date when the designs were created and the type of design, which is NewBuild.",ox:"Label for grouping a set of NewBuild designs by time. Each group name contains the time of the current day when the designs were created and the type of design, which is NewBuild.",Z7:"Label for grouping a set of Solar designs by date. Each group name contains the date when the designs were created and the type of design, which is Solar.",K1:"Label for grouping a set of Solar designs by time. Each group name contains the time of the current day when the designs were created and the type of design, which is Solar.",Xm:"Label for text field that allows editing of the currently selected feature's description.",Ta:"Label for text field that allows editing of the currently selected feature's title.",yL:"Label for text field that shows the range of number of floors in floor group in a building if max is 1.",Pe:"Label for text field that shows the range of number of floors in floor group in a building.",gI:"Label for the Paste option in a context menu for a project, specifically referring to a copied feature.",dv:"Label for the Paste option in the menu bar or a context menu, specifically referring to a copied feature.",hz:"Label for the Paste option in the menu bar or a context menu.",pJ:"Label for the Select Folder contents option in the overflow menu bar for a folder.",CE:"Label for the approximate summed area of a set of features of a given type in a project, which allows users to understand the information items they see in the insepector panel. The summed area is shown when users select multiple features of different types and the information item is shown for the same feature type.",AT:"Label for the approximate summed length of a set of features of a given type in a project, which allows users to understand the information items they see in the insepector panel. The summed length is shown when users select multiple features of different types and the information item is shown for the same feature type.",Zj:"Label for the area measured on the globe while using the measurement tool. Only shown if the user has drawn a closed polygon.",Xs:"Label for the community use type, which could include recreation centers.",un:"Label for the dialog action button that clears data cache.",EH:"Label for the dialog action button that clears domains list.",nx:"Label for the dialog action button that clears search history.",tQ:"Label for the education use type, which could include schools or universities.",tp:"Label for the green space use type, which could include parks.",pw:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at -23 latitude.",Ib:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at -66 latitude.",GO:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at 0 longitude.",AO:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at 180 longitude.",hi:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at 23 latitude.",GL:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at 66 latitude.",At:"Label for the gridline that is on the globe at zero latitude.",A4:"Label for the loading button that appears when discarding drafts, which are unfinished sets of inputs for a design.",JL:"Label for the menu item that allows users to request an update to the satellite or aerial imagery for a specific location.",of:"Label for the office use type, which could include office buildings.",eD:"Label for the parking ratio entry type that allows users to enter parking ratios per 100 m\xb2 (e.g. 10 parking spots per 100 m\xb2). m\xb2 stands for square meters.",S1:"Label for the parking ratio entry type that allows users to enter parking ratios per 1000 ft\xb2 (e.g. 10 parking spots per 1000 ft\xb2). ft\xb2 stands for square feet.",yg:"Label for the parking ratio entry type that allows users to enter parking ratios per unit. Unit refers to a residential unit (e.g. a building with 100 residential units). The parking ratio allows users to set the number of parking spots per unit (e.g. 1 parking spot per 5 residential units).",Or:"Label for the residential use type, which could include apartment complexes.",Cp:"Label for the retail use type, which could include shopping centers.",zn:"Label in settings for denoting the current version of the app.",L8:"Label in settings for denoting the region setting which shows the country code the user is from.",Lz:"Label in the document view indicating that the number of features in the document is close to the limit.",z5:"Label in the document view indicating that the number of features in the document is over the limit.",GX:"Label in the flow to generate new built environment designs that represents one of the unit mixes for a building whose use type is Hotel. Unit mixes are the different types of units that will be in the building (e.g. hotel room, hotel suite).",In:"Label in the flow to generate new built environment designs that represents one of the unit mixes for a building whose use type is Residential. Unit mixes are the different types of units that will be in the building (e.g. studio, 1 bedroom, 2 bedroom, 3 bedroom).",NB:"Label indicating that an item's data is being refreshed.",po:"Label indicating that the 'Magic camera' feature is part of an experimental release.",Ww:"Label indicating that the current project has been saved on this device's local storage, not in Google Drive.",fu:"Label notifying the user that their project is empty.",iW:"Label of a button allowing the user to allow a certain domain for the purposes of loading KML.",PO:"Label of a button allowing the user to disallow a certain domain for the purposes of loading KML.",KD:"Label of a button allowing the user to sign in to their account",b4:"Label of a button for downloading a 3D Buildings image that is associated with a design. The filetype is a common image format called PNG which stands for Portable Network Graphics.",MR:"Label of a button for downloading a 3D Solar Panels image that is associated with a design.",hc:"Label of a button for downloading a Parti Diagram Image that is associated with a design.",vf:"Label of a button for downloading a Rhino file that is associated with a design. Rhino is a software product commonly used in architecture, design, and construction. The file type, called 3DM, stands for 3-dimensional model.",Ui:"Label of a button for downloading a financial model that is associated with a design.",nc:"Label of a button for downloading an AutoCAD DXF file that is associated with a design. DXF stands for drawing exchange format and is a vector file format used for design drawings in 2D and 3D.",mT:"Label of a button for downloading an image.",qs:"Label of a button for downloading design artifacts and data tables, generated geometries, images, and financial models.",hv:"Label of a button for exporting a site study design to a Google Earth map.",Cl:"Label of a button in a banner shown at the top of the viewport introducing the new version of Earth.  When clicked, the button will take the user to a Google Earth Help Center article explaining the changes.",_y:"Label of a button in a dialog inviting the user to explore the Voyager showcase, which will open in a new tab",rD:"Label of a button in a dialog inviting the user to open the Basemap Settings panel, which will show the Timelapse layer",iJ:"Label of a button in a dialog that will finish the user import output selection.",PZ:"Label of a button in a toast that will continue the user action that was interrupted.",ON:"Label of a button in a toast that will retry the failed config request.",YJ:"Label of a button in a toast that will retry the failed user request.",ft:"Label of a button that allows the user to copy a link to the current design to their clipboard.",sz:"Label of a button that finishes the site selection step.",jF:"Label of a button that lets the user choose a building analysis study from the two possible study types.",mo:"Label of a button that lets the user choose a solar study from the two possible study types",n:"Label of a button that lets the user save the feature (a dropped pin, a Knowledge Card, or a measurement) to a new or existing document.",jY:"Label of a button that lets the user select a custom color for the feature they are editing",RD:"Label of a button that lets the user show an expanded view of their most recent searches.",pj:"Label of a button that will allow a user to skip or bypass a step.",Zz:"Label of a button used to generate a new image.  For example in the 'Magic camera' feature.",_7:"Label of a control which toggles the Photos layer on or off. This message should be as short as possible.",cw:"Label of a dropdown field for the development program entry target type, which can be entered either as a target value or minimum and maximum values.",IL:"Label of a dropdown field for the development program entry unit type, which can be entered either floor area ratio or area (sq m or sq ft).",s4:"Label of a dropdown menu allowing the user to select a grounding mode, also known as an altitude mode. This is a tricky term to translate, but essentially it defines a reference surface from which a point's altitude should be measured, along with whether the point is allowed to be floating above that surface or should be forcibly placed directly onto it.",rc:"Label of a header that describes the function of the design feature in Earth",we:"Label of a header that encourages the user to start create a site by selecting a tax lot or draw a shape.",Ev:"Label of a menu item allowing the user to add a photo using from the photo library on their phone.",iw:"Label of a menu item allowing the user to add a photo using the camera on their phone. Note that unlike other uses of this word, in this case we are talking about a physical camera device on a phone, not an abstract camera view inside the app.",Wd:"Label of a net metering preference option in the Financials step of the create solar study workflow. All refers to full net metering, which means that all energy generated from solar panels will be sold to the grid.",xb:"Label of a net metering preference option in the Financials step of the create solar study workflow. Excess refers to partial net metering, which means that only extra energy generated from solar panels will be sold to the grid.",Ie:"Label of a net metering preference option in the Financials step of the create solar study workflow. Net metering allows property owners with solar panels to get credits for generating excess electricity and reducing energy costs.",cK:"Label of a popup menu item allowing the user to select a text style for their feature description.  Heading is a large header style.  See Google Docs for equivalent strings.",px:"Label of a popup menu item allowing the user to select a text style for their feature description.  Selecting Normal Text removes any previously applied header style.  See Google Docs for equivalent strings.",yq:"Label of a popup menu item allowing the user to select a text style for their feature description.  Subheading is a small header style.  See Google Docs for equivalent strings.",hN:"Label of a popup menu item allowing the user to select a text style for their feature description.  Title is the largest and most prominent header style.  See Google Docs for equivalent strings.",Ow:"Label of a switch controlling whether modifiers (like alt or control) will be required for all keyboard shortcuts",a:"Label of a text banner indicating that the shown feature is available as part of the experimental launch. This is used in features when they are in the experimental phase, like Design & Development, EarthMate, Contour Analysis tool, etc.",ru:"Label of a text button that clears search history when clicked.",Ne:"Label of a toast action the user can invoke to allow a network connection to an untrusted server.",oH:"Label of a toast indicating that the full error log from the Error Guide has been copied to the clipboard.",CI:"Label of a tooltip that describes the Geospatial Design feature suite, which does indeed contain real estate and clean energy development tools",s1:"Label of several financial assumptions fields.",NJ:"Label of the Buildings step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",LI:"Label of the Development program subsection of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. Development program refers to the ...",N2:"Label of the Energy Use field for capturing estimated electricity use.",HS:"Label of the Energy Use field for capturing estimated fuel use.",w2:"Label of the Energy Use field that sums the energy use total.",KA:"Label of the Financials field for capturing estimated electricity rate.",f8:"Label of the Financials field for capturing the electricity rate escalator value.",Fd:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the PPA price escalator. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",t1:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the PPA price. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",Ke:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the building roof cost.",bq:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the building roof monthly lease.",Uv:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the debt fraction.",Rs:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the lease rate escalator.",X9:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the loan rate.",d_:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the net metering preference.",DV:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the parking lot cost.",D_:"Label of the Financials field for the value of the parking lot monthly lease.",Qx:"Label of the Green space subsection of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. Users can indicate how much of a site or parcel they want to be dedicated to green space, such as parks.",qh:"Label of the Metrics step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",uw:"Label of the Program step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. Development program refers to the proportion of each use type that is developed on each site or parcel.",Wq:"Label of the Use Types step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",MU:"Label of the Use types dropdown selector for floor groups in the building editor dialog. A use type describes the floor's intended usage such as being used for residential, office, or retail space.",Xz:"Label on a legend in the map showing that the categories in the legend is by apartment type, e.g. 'Studio', 'One Bedroom', or 'Two Bedroom'.",Kf:"Label on a legend in the map showing that the categories in the legend is by building use type, e.g. 'Residential', 'Office', or 'Commercial'.",Jt:"Label on a legend in the map showing that the categories in the legend is by sunlight hours.",X_:"Label on a legend in the map showing that the categories in the legend is views.",fk:"Label on a legend in the map showing that the legend item represents a park.",RZ:"Label on a legend in the map showing that the legend item represents a road.",Gm:"Label on a legend in the map that shows the type of the legend indicating the amount of energy from solar flux received on roofs.",zJ:"Label or tooltip for a button which shows a dropdown menu containing additional actions.",UV:"Label showing the user that their project changes could not be saved because they are offline.",qP:"Label showing the user that their project had errors while saving to storage, and that they are advised to reload.",AW:"Label showing the user that their project is currently being saved to storage.",Ii:"Label shown in a menu that allows the user to download the selected KML file in Earth as a KML file.",x2:"Label shown in a menu that allows the user to export the selected item as a KML file.",Ey:"Label shown in the copy document dialog notifying the user that selected the document is currently loading.",jo:"Label shown in the copy document dialog notifying the user that the document is being copied.",iq:"Label shown in the search field inviting the user to search for layers in the data catalog.",AC:"Label shown in the search field inviting the user to search for places they want to explore.",IY:"Label shown in the search field of the command palette, inviting the user to search for commands (such as menu items) by name.",f:"Label shown on a button that allows the user to edit the contents of a place in the My Places view. This string should be kept as short as possible, ideally no more than five or six characters. Abbreviations may be necessary in some languages. Please file a ticket if you have questions or concerns.",Hn:"Label shown on a button that allows the user to select from a large list of icons.  The icons chosen this way are applied to point placemarks on the globe.",Pi:"Label shown on a button that allows the user to switch which Google account they are signed in with.",ia:"Label shown on a button that allows the user to upload a custom icon.  The icon will be applied to a point placemark on the globe.",KN:"Label shown on a button that takes the user to the playstore/appstore to update the Google Earth application.",UO:'Label shown on a popup menu that allows the user to select the size of an icon from a predefined set of values including "small" and "large".',B2:"Label shown to describe what balloon content created with an unsupported panel type will look like.",cZ:'Label shown to describe what balloon content created with the "None" panel type will look like.',Qm:"Label shown to describe what balloon content created with the card template will look like.",sN:"Label shown to describe what balloon content created with the panel template will look like.",I6:"Label telling the user that they are filtering projects based on last modified time.",jG:"Label telling the user that they are filtering projects based on owner.",Xv:"Label text for a dropdown menu item that allows the user to delete a building type from the building editor view.",OI:"Label that indicates that a Earth subscription plan is available as part of an experimental release.",_E:"Label that indicates the selected Google Cloud Project is what will will be used for billing.",gE:"Label that indicates the user will use Earth without a selected Google Cloud Project.",IO:"Label to indicate that the values users enter apply to the entire site total program targets.",UM:"Label used for a menu item that allows the user to edit the current project's description.",Mh:"Label used for a tooltip on the share button in the toolbar that opens the share dialog to share a link.",qy:"Label used for a tooltip on the share button in the toolbar when that button is disabled.",u8:"Label used for a tooltip, menu item, and dialog that allow the user to edit the current project's name and description.",p:"Label used for the share button in the toolbar that opens the share dialog to share a link.",oP:"Land and coastal ecosystems management / conservation",Gt:"Large option in the size selector for points and labels in a layer.",LC:"Large option of the label style size selector.",xK:"Layers imported by other users and designs will not be included in the copy.",ry:"Leaving this plan will mean losing access to premium features.",EA:"Linear ring must have three distinct coordinates",Y2:"Linear ring with distinct first and last coordinates",L3:"Link name in the Account Particle Disc on Web to sign out",lS:"Load large datasets quickly to see trends (features read-only)",zR:"Long press to rotate for a longer distance",iB:"Longer text explaining a toggle button allowing the user to change from a graphic user interface optimized for desktop computers (large screen typically with keyboard and mouse) to an interface optimized for mobile devices (phones and tablets).",vm:"Longer text explaining a toggle button allowing the user to change from a graphic user interface optimized for mobile devices (phones and tablets) to an interface optimized for desktop computers (large screen typically with keyboard and mouse).",j6:"Manage changes with dedicated buttons in the toolbar and keyboard shortcuts",UT:"Marker shown on KML based projects, helping the user discern Cloud based projects and KML files. Also used as a tooltip for a KML icon.",SY:"Max height will limit the height of buildings in this parcel.",I:"Max stands for maximum. This value labels fields that are used to set a maximum area or percentage value for a use type, parcel or site.",bf:"Maximum building height, floor-area ratio (FAR), building coverage ratio (BCR), open space ratio (OSR), and street setbacks are currently supported.",Z2:"Measurements and values will be displayed using this unit system unless specific units are selected for distance or area.",ya:"Medium option in the size selector for points and labels in a layer.",xm:"Menu item for when the user chooses to edit a class for classification layers.",j1:'Menu item label that lets the user copy the ID of the selected feature.  The "feature ID" is a special concept that can be assumed to be understood by anyone who needs to use this menu item.',sJ:"Menu item label that lets the user copy the selected project.",eH:"Menu item lets the user draw lines or shapes on the map.",_C:"Menu item that hides the selected features in a project on the earth.",lA:"Menu item that opens a dropdown of the various site assessment analysis tools. Site assessment refers to the process of evaluating a piece of land for a specific purpose, such as construction or development.",s5:"Menu item that opens the aspect analysis view. Aspect analysis is a tool that allows users to analyze the aspect of their site. Aspect refers to the direction the slope is facing.",UK:"Menu item that opens the available data layers dialog, which allows users to select from data layers to add to their project.",L5:"Menu item that opens the classify with AI tool, which allows users to categorize the basemap based on user-defined classes and sample points.",o:"Menu item that opens the contour analysis view. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain.",O5:"Menu item that opens the cut and fill analysis view. Cut and fill analysis is a process that measures the volume of earth material that needs to be moved to create a level area of land.",EP:"Menu item that opens the slope analysis view. Slope analysis is a tool that allows users to analyze the slope of their site. Slope refers to the steepness of the terrain.",RE:"Menu item that shows the selected features in a project on the earth.",WH:"Menu item to select a cinematic type of animation at the end of a camera fly-to transition.",vJ:"Menu item to select a medium speed for camera animations in Google Earth.",LJ:"Menu item to select an orbital type of animation at the end of a camera fly-to transition.",i3:"Menu item to select no animation at the end of a camera fly-to transition.",wK:"Menu item to select slightly faster camera animations in Google Earth.",BP:"Menu item to select slightly slower camera animations in Google Earth.",Of:"Menu item to select the fastest possible camera animations in Google Earth.",Wr:"Menu item to select the slowest possible camera animations in Google Earth.",NC:"Menu item under Rendering quality that sets slightly faster rendering settings in Google Earth.",oA:"Menu item under Rendering quality that sets slightly higher-quality rendering settings in Google Earth.",IV:"Menu item under Rendering quality that sets the default quality for rendering settings in Google Earth.",EG:"Menu item under Rendering quality that sets the fastest possible rendering settings in Google Earth.",JZ:"Menu item under Rendering quality that sets the highest-quality rendering settings in Google Earth.",ej:"Menu item which will cause the camera to fly to and orbit around a specified latitude and longitude.",d6:"Menu item which will cause the camera to recenter the visible viewport on a specified latitude and longitude.",VY:"Menu item which will copy the coordinates of a specified point on the map into the clipboard.  Usually this will be a latitude/longitude pair, but we may support other reference systems someday.",C_:"Menu option that allows the user to delete the currently selected project.",mN:"Menu option which will cause the camera to fly to a specified latitude and longitude.",UE:"Message informing users that there are no recent search terms.",mf:"Message of a toast shown when a user requests access to a project, and the request succeeds.",Z3:"Message shown in a dialog when the user tries to export a document as a KML file. This message explains that the user can still share their project through Google Drive to collaborate with others in the cloud even if some features cannot be exported.",Ya:"Message shown in a status tracker indicating that a design import is complete.",za:"Message shown when the cache has been cleared.",q3:"Message shown when the settings have been reset.",xG:"Message that is displayed when an error occurred while fetching the AI generated area description. A refresh button is also shown next to the message, prompting the user to press it.",f1:"Metrics determine how designs will be ranked in this study.",uN:"Min - Max refers to setting both a minimum and a maximum value of the gross floor area. The generated designs will aim to have the actual gross floor area value be between the minimum and maximum values set by the user.",L:"Min stands for minimum. This value labels fields that are used to set a minimum area or percentage value for a use type, parcel or site.",p9:"Move smoothly across the globe when flying to a destination.",yA:"Move the map and add points to draw a path or polygon boundary",oy:"Move the map and add points to measure distances and area",Ej:"Move the map to place the cursor where you want to enter Street View.",yd:"Move the map to where you want to drop the placemark",Wg:"NOTIFICATIONS_ENROLLMENT_AFTER_FEELING_LUCKY_ENABLED",qZ:"NOTIFICATIONS_ENROLLMENT_AFTER_VOYAGER_STORY_ENABLED",ZV:"Name in dropdown menu of attribute type Boolean",M3:"Name in dropdown menu of attribute type Decimal number",mi:"Name in dropdown menu of attribute type Integer",N8:"Name in dropdown menu of attribute type String",y:"Name of Google Earth's AI assistant feature. It is shown as a title in the UI and as the tooltip for opening the feature.",JX:'Name of a Map Style that can be edited by the user ("customized") to hide selected base layer feature categories, such as roads, and names. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=54206',eS:"Name of a Map Style that hides all base layer feature categories, such as roads, borders and names. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=55782",rq:"Name of a Map Style that shows a particular set of base layer feature categories (specifically roads, borders and names) that we consider well-suited for exploring the map, while hiding some other categories (e.g. POIs) to minimize clutter. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=54210",pH:"Name of a Map Style that shows all possible base layer feature categories, roads, borders and names. Please leverage https://tc.corp.google.com/btviewer/messagedetail?project=gws&msgId=54208",RC:"Name of a downloadable 3D Buildings Image that is associated with a design. Used for constructing the file name of the download.",qr:"Name of a downloadable 3D Solar Panels Image that is associated with a design. Used for constructing the file name of the download.",sR:"Name of a downloadable AutoCAD DXF file that is associated with a design. Used for constructing the file name of the download. DXF stands for drawing exchange format and is a vector file format used for design drawings in 2D and 3D",Uw:"Name of a downloadable Parti Diagram Image that is associated with a design. Used for constructing the file name of the download.",Ir:"Name of a downloadable Rhino file that is associated with a design. Used for constructing the file name of the download. Rhino is a software product commonly used in architecture, design, and construction. The file type, called 3DM, stands for 3-dimensional model",ug:"Name of a downloadable financial model that is associated with a design. Used for constructing the file name of the download.",Q4:"Name of a general layer that is created on-demand, as opposed to being pre-generated. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a map.",JC:"Name of a map style that shows a shaded terrain relief.",yt:"Name of a map style that shows a simplified roadmap without the realistic details of satellite and aerial images.",Ov:"Name of a map style that shows highly detailed satellite and aerial images.",vQ:"Name of the 'Professional Advanced' Earth subscription plan.",ZR:"Name of the 'Professional' Earth subscription plan.",Rf:"Name of the 'Standard' Earth subscription plan.",ei:"Nature-based solutions (e.g. voluntary carbon market, carbon removals, monitoring, reporting, and verification)",vB:"Need to view this data layer? Upgrade now.",Az:"Net Metering Preference will be used to indicate how credits will be received from sending energy from solar panels to the grid if applicable.",cg:"Net metering allows property owners with solar panels to get credits for generating excess electricity and reducing energy costs.",hQ:"No sustainability strategies have been applied to this design.",cA:"Node already has a parent, copy or remove it first",iF:"Not applicable: net metering is not supported",ae:"Note, some visible imagery has unknown date information.",Ou:"ON_DEMAND_EVALUATION_CUT_AND_FILL_ENABLED",oC:"ON_DEMAND_EVALUATION_SLOPE_AND_ASPECT_ENABLED",Ul:"One or more provided geometries do not conform to S2 restrictions.",tM:"Only JPEG, PNG, SVG and HEIF/HEIC images are currently supported.",W_:"Only one layer can be generated at a time",P4:"Only project owners can import data layers into their projects. This feature is experimental and affects their storage quota.",hg:"Only projects on Google Drive can be shared",T2:"Open an existing file you can save in your browser",ST:"Open an existing file you can save on your device",j8:"Open files from Google Earth Pro and other GIS apps to edit them here. Enjoy a streamlined workflow with the power of Google Earth's imagery on web, while keeping your data on your device \u2013 no cloud upload required.",o4:"Opportunities to participate in user research and pilot new features to improve Google Earth",uO:"Option for filtering by last modified time. Gets all projects that have been modified in the last 24 hours.",no:"Option in the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to enable parking in basements (e.g. underground parking garages).",pe:"Option in the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to enable parking on surfaces (e.g. parking lots).",rM:"Option in the sort menu when viewing a list of Built Environment designs. This option is for organizing the designs by overall score in descending order, with the best scoring design appearing first. The overall score is a quantified metric that measures the design quality.",t8:"Option in the sort menu when viewing a list of Built Environment designs. This option is for organizing the designs by update time in ascending order.",TT:"Option in the sort menu when viewing a list of Built Environment designs. This option is for organizing the designs by update time in descending order.",cf:"Other images are not available here. Try different locations to find Street View historical imagery and explore changes over time.",Y3:"Parameter `useAreaLandUnit` is only supported for AREA units.",MX:"Parcel target refers to the target value of the gross floor area for each individual parcel contained in a site.",VB:"Parsing error due to <kml> tag not being the first element, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",bS:"Parsing error due to KMZ file not containing a KML file, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",qo:"Parsing error due to an incorrect encoding, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",If:"Parsing error due to an invalid XML heading, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",Bz:"Parsing error due to the KMZ file could not be opened, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",LK:"Parsing error due to the KMZ file referencing an external file, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",Y4:"Parsing error due to the XML declaration not being first, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",sd:"Parsing error due to the file heading not being UTF-8, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",VO:"Parsing error due to the issues with opening the ZIP file.",O9:"Parsing error due to unexpected data after closing </kml> tag, displayed in Error Guide during file import.",s_:"Part of a bulleted list of features that cannot be exported to KML. This is show below the exportAsKmlDialogWarningMessage when a document contains designs.",uk:"Part of the version label in settings About that indicates if the app is multi-threaded. The word goes right after the version number, for instance: 10.1.2.3 Multi-threaded.",U_:"Part of the version label in settings About that indicates if the app is single-threaded. The word goes right after the version number, for instance: 10.1.2.3 Single-threaded.",pz:"Paste operation failed. Are you signed in?",Iz:"Paste the URL of an image or YouTube video here to add it to your feature.",Eo:'PathMetricIterator is not pointing to a PathMetric. This can happen in two situations:\n- The iteration has not started yet. If so, call "moveNext" to start iteration.\n- The iterator ran out of elements. If so, check that "moveNext" returns true prior to calling "current".',Ae:"People who have access to this project will see this info about you.",Vv:"Percentages refers to how users will set a minimum and a maximum value of green space for a site or parcel. The generated designs will aim to have the actual percentage of the site or parcel that has green space be between the minimum and maximum percentage values set by the user.",m9:"Placeholder prompt for the 'Create images' feature.",n8:"Placeholder text for the designs list when no designs are available.",kA:"Placeholder text shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat prompt field encouraging the user to ask a follow up prompt.",Ko:"Placeholder text shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat prompt field encouraging the user to prompt it.",s9:"Plan details for design features included in the 'Standard' Earth subscription plan, shown in a view to choose plans",Dk:"Plan details for more features to come in the 'Professional' and 'Professional Advanced' Earth subscription plan, shown in a view to choose plans.",vy:"Please fix all errors to generate designs.",wE:"Primary text of a banner shown at the top of the viewport informing the user that a new home screen for Google Earth is coming soon.",Kx:"Progress towards loading current satellite imagery",jP:"Prompt for a tab that allows the user to filter data layers by the area of the selected features. The user must select data layers to filter.",vg:"Prompt for selecting an area for a classification layer. Classification layers use AI to categorize the basemap into different classes based on user-defined sample points.",fZ:"Radio button label shown in the sharing dialog for an Earth Feed/ Voyager story that selects sharing a link to the top of the story rather than to the current chapter. I.e. it selects sharing the story as a whole rather than a particular point within the story.",VH:"Radio button label shown in the sharing dialog for an Earth Feed/Voyager story that selects sharing a link to the particular chapter within the story, rather than to the top of the story.",Ud:"Real estate & clean energy development tools",tJ:"Recreate this map in the style of an old treasure map",BO:"Reduced parking limits the estimated vehicle distance traveled, reducing overall emissions by ",Z4:"Reference project data is only visible to you.",bs:"Reference project data is only visible to you. It won\u2019t be included when you share your project with others.",iD:"Refine inputs to generate more designs like this",aN:"Remove zoning requirement refers to removing an existing zoning requirement from a land parcel.",XF:"Request access, or switch to an account with access.",Al:"Request sent. You'll get an email if access is granted.",Lr:"Required refers to whether a use type is required to be included in the development.",RL:"Row header for parking metrics in the design details tables.",mY:"START_WITH_NEW_DRAFT_REQUEST_STATE_CREATE_FAILURE",RG:"START_WITH_NEW_DRAFT_REQUEST_STATE_CREATE_PENDING",Hm:"START_WITH_NEW_DRAFT_REQUEST_STATE_DISCARD_FAILURE",Ad:"START_WITH_NEW_DRAFT_REQUEST_STATE_DISCARD_PENDING",RJ:"START_WITH_NEW_DRAFT_REQUEST_STATE_SUCCESS",vU:"START_WITH_NEW_DRAFT_REQUEST_STATE_UNSPECIFIED",rE:"Schema missing an ID. Please assign a unique ID.",Vd:"Screen reader hint on a widget that allows the user to set a color's saturation and value by panning",f7:"Screen reader label of the editor view, which allows the user to edit information such as when a slide is created.",Hj:"Screen reader label of the inspector view, which allows the user to see information about a specific feature or object on the globe",_l:"Screen reader label on a widget that allows the user to set a color's saturation and value by panning.",Lp:"Secondary text of a banner shown at the top of the viewport informing the user that a new home screen for Google Earth is coming soon.",N0:"Section header for viewing built environment designs belonging to a project.",Lc:"Section label shown on the Filter tab of the Data Layer Details panel when an area filter has been applied to a data layer.",NK:"Section of the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to enable various parking strategies. Parking strategies refers to things like enabling surface or basement parking lots.",zo:"Section of the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to set an area for parking spots (e.g. a parking spot is 10 sq m)",HO:"Section of the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to set parking ratios per building use type (e.g. for my residential building, I want 1 parking spot per 100 sq m).",__:"See data that falls within a specified area",bW:"See more dates with Street View historical imagery and explore how locations change over time.",_Z:"See the latest image and hide other dates",tC:"Segmented button label for the fast playback speed (2x) in the Timelapse video feature, as in [twice the normal speed].",Ra:"Segmented button label for the medium playback speed (1x) in the Timelapse video feature, as in [1 times the normal speed].",L1:"Segmented button label for the slow playback speed (0.5x) in the Timelapse video feature, as in [0.5 times the normal speed].",ze:"Segmented button tooltip for the fast playback speed (2x) in the Timelapse video feature.",e8:"Segmented button tooltip for the medium playback speed (1x) in the Timelapse video feature.",uC:"Segmented button tooltip for the slow playback speed (0.5x) in the Timelapse video feature.",w3:"Select a project from the dropdown below to access premium features",fT:"Select one or more parcels to define your site. You\u2019ll be able to set a development program and zoning for each parcel.",pa:"Select or draw your parcels for your site.",HX:"Selection of the presentation dropdown menu to select a large panel.",Rr:"Selection of the presentation dropdown menu to select a small card.",_b:"Selection of the presentation dropdown menu to select no card or panel.",MW:"Semantic label explaining that a project is owned by an unknown person.",jm:"Semantic label explaining that a project was last modified at an unknown date or time.",tX:"Semantic label for a button that allows the user to download all design artifacts and data tables, generated geometries, images, and financial models.",Z8:"Semantic label for a data table row that indicates that the row is selected.",zH:"Semantic label for a dropdown menu in building editor view. The dropdown menu allows the user to delete a building type from the building editor view.",Ok:"Semantic label for a generic loading spinner.",dZ:"Semantic label for a loading bar that indicates that the request for a list of data rows is in progress.",Fi:"Semantic label for a loading spinner that indicates that the request for a list of data layers is in progress.",Le:"Semantic label for a loading spinner that indicates that the request for a list of designs is in progress.",dc:"Semantic label for a loading spinner that indicates that the request for the design details is in progress.",ZT:"Semantic label for a parcel analysis error icon when the area size is invalid, e.g. too large or too small.",Wo:"Semantic label for the development program entry type, which can be entered either as a target value or minimum and maximum values.",Gf:"Semantic label for the drag indicator in the building editor displayed on each floor group tile. The user can drag the floor group tile to reorder the floor groups in the building configuration. This label is meant for specifiying to the users that the floor group tile can be dragged. A floor group is a set of floors that share the same configuration.",PC:"Semantic label for the green space entry type, which can be entered either as a percentage of an area or in acres.",A5:"Semantic label for the parking ratio entry type, which can be entered either as a number of spots per residential unit or per area.",CM:"Semantic label of a button that refresh the projects list.",nj:"Semantics label for 0 bytes of storage used.",T9:"Semantics label for Screen Readers to notify the users they are focusing the Search suggestions.",iS:"Semantics label for a checkbox that is not selected.",Cr:"Semantics label for a checkbox that is selected.",Ps:"Semantics label for screen readers to notify the users they are focusing the Projects panel.",fJ:"Semantics label for screen readers to notify the users they are focusing the parcel section in the site selection panel.",LR:"Semantics label for screen readers to notify the users they are focusing the site analysis section in the site selection panel.",iK:"Semantics label for screen readers to notify the users they are focusing the site area description section in the site selection panel.",Br:"Semantics label for screen readers to notify the users they are focusing the site selection panel.",mP:"Semantics label for the design generation status pane in the left hand panel",Dl:"Semantics label for the status pane in the left hand panel that indicates what operations are underway (e.g. file import, contour layer generation, etc.)",Jf:"Semantics label for the style section in the layer details panel.",o3:"Set ratios for each use type. Larger numbers will increase the amount of parking in each design option.",sv:"Share your project through Google Drive to collaborate on the full contents in the cloud.",hr:"Short description for a settings action that clears Earth's data cache.",G3:"Short description for a settings action that clears the list of allowed and blocked domains.",a1:"Short label for a toggle button allowing the user to change from a graphic user interface optimized for desktop computers (large screen typically with keyboard and mouse) to an interface optimized for mobile devices (phones and tablets).",Cn:"Short label for a toggle button allowing the user to change from a graphic user interface optimized for mobile devices (phones and tablets) to an interface optimized for desktop computers (large screen typically with keyboard and mouse).",vT:"Show 3D buildings and trees where available.",Y9:"Show areas where 3D data such as buildings and trees are available.",RK:"Show areas where satellite or aerial imagery has been most recently updated.",wW:"Shown as a notification to the user that their search history has been cleared.",cr:"Shown as a title in the Google Drive file picker.",xw:"Shown as the title of the Pinned Projects dialog.",af:"Shown in the search results panel when there are no search results for current query.",cF:"Shown in the search results panel when there are no search suggestions for current query.",D9:"Shown when the heating electrification sustainability strategy has been applied to the design. Electrification refers to the process of switching from non-electric to electric power sources. This is shown in the emissions summary table in the design details panel.",dP:"Shown when the no sustinability strategies have been applied to the design. This is shown in the emissions summary table in the design details panel.",uV:"Shown when the reduced parking strategy has been applied. Reduced parking reduces estimated automobile miles traveled which then reduces overall emissions. This is shown in the emissions summary table in the design details panel.",Nu:"Shown when the solar panels were use in the building design. When solar is used, there is an operational energy offset which leads to a reduction in emissions. This is shown in the emissions summary table in the design details panel.",fX:"Shown when the sustainability materials strategy has been applied to calculte the emissions saved from materials used. This is shown in the emissions summary table in the design details panel.",hf:"Site design is unavailable in local KML files",k1:"Site target refers to the target value of the gross floor area for the entire site.",Vq:"Sitewide program FAR target must be above ",Ji:"Slope estimatation label for a text field above the slope statistics. Slope is defined as the ratio of the change in elevation to the change in horizontal distance.",Gc:"Small option in the size selector for points and labels in a layer.",FU:"Small option of the label style size selector.",aS:"Snackbar text indicating that location services are disabled at the device level.",Wm:"Snackbar text indicating that location tracking has been denied.",HC:"Snackbar text indicating that the system failed (timed out) while trying to fetch the device's GPS location.",VR:"Some data may be hidden, zoom in for better results",VT:"Some features won't be included in export",zz:"Some of your changes may not be saved. Please reload Google Earth after continuing.",Zp:"Sorry, features can\u2019t be moved between projects \u2014 yet!",H:"Statement presented in the full error log for an import",OT:"Status label next to a long running action in a status tracker, like a file import or design generation, indicating that the action completed.",o8:"Status label next to a long running action in a status tracker, like a file import or design generation, indicating that the action failed.",Ez:"Status label next to a long running action in a status tracker, like a file import or design generation, indicating that the action has been cancelled by the user.",Va:"Status text for a section that indicates that a contour analysis layer is being created. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain.",pG:"Status text for a section that indicates that a slope analysis layer is being created. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map. Slope refers to the steepness of the terrain.",ef:"Status text for a section that indicates that an aspect analysis layer is being created. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map. Aspect refers to the direction that a slope is facing.",gS:"Stored in Google Drive, so you can share with others and open from any device",ur:"Stored only on your browser or device. Files will be deleted if you clear your app data.",E:"Stream has been disposed.\nAn ImageStream is considered disposed once at least one listener has been added and subsequently all listeners have been removed and no handles are outstanding from the keepAlive method.\nTo resolve this error, maintain at least one listener on the stream, or create an ImageStreamCompleterHandle from the keepAlive method, or create a new stream for the image.",VA:"Subheader for the entrypoint to the area filter tool in the Filter tab of the Data Layer Details panel.",an:"Subheading of the 'Standard' Earth subscription plan, shown above plan details in a view to choose plans",QR:"Subtitle at the top right of the Data Table, indicating if the table shows data that is within the current view.",QB:"Subtitle displayed in the Data Table if there are no features visible in the current viewport prompting the user to pan (move the map around) or zoom in or out.",_w:"Subtitle displayed in the Data Table if there was a generic error while fetching or displaying data for the data table, prompting the user to try again.",YA:"Subtitle explaining the area showing advanced settings for building use types. Use types refer to how the building will be used (e.g. for residential or hotel purposes).",y_:"Subtitle for a section that allows the user to define an area for analysis by drawing or selecting a physical polygon on the earth for the purpose of analyzing data layers in that area.",GG:"Subtitle for a toggle button to cloud animations in Google Earth.",Kr:"Subtitle for a toggle button to enable 3D buildings in Google Earth.",V8:"Subtitle for a toggle button to enable 3D coverage layer in Google Earth.",Yd:"Subtitle for a toggle button to enable recently updated satellite or aerial imagery layer in Google Earth.",H6:"Subtitle for a toggle button to enable the Historical Imagery feature.",E9:"Subtitle for a toggle button to gridlines in Google Earth.",zU:"Subtitle for an item in the Earth Mate onboarding dialog.",Xg:"Subtitle for graphics rendering quality selection in the settings panel.",Ug:"Subtitle for the data layer option in the user import output selector dialog.",kV:"Subtitle for the financial assumptions section of the Financials step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",RQ:"Subtitle for the lease or ppa assumptions section of the Financials step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",yT:"Subtitle for the map features option in the user import output selector dialog.",mG:"Subtitle for the purchase or loan assumptions section of the Financials step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",WX:"Subtitle of a card inviting the user to interact with the Data Catalog in Google Earth and explaining that the data layers are included with Professional and Professional Advanced plans.",HV:"Subtitle of a control which toggles the Photos layer on or off. This message should be as short as possible.",vR:"Subtitle of a dialog that allows the user to add a KML file to a new or an existing Google Earth project.",co:"Subtitle of a dialog that shows the data layers that are available to add to the current project.",Tq:"Subtitle of a status tracker indicating that a design is being imported and may take a minute.",LH:"Subtitle of the Energy Use step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",zh:"Subtitle of the Metrics step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",Pc:"Subtitle of the Site (e.g. a land area) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. The tip informs the user that adding zoning requirements will help ensure that their designs are feasible.",ul:"Subtitle of the Use Types tab when entering inputs to New Build designs. Use types refers to how the building will be used (e.g. for residential or commercial purposes).",Dy:"Subtitle of the parking spot area section in the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs that allows users to set an area for parking spots (e.g. a parking spot is 10 sq m)",ZW:"Suffix of several financial assumptions fields.",nn:"Suffix of the Energy Use field for capturing estimated fuel use.",mS:"Suffix shown at the end of a numerical edit field for kilowatt hours during design generation.",ob:"Suffix shown at the end of a numerical edit field for price of kilowatt hours during design generation.",nI:"Summary description describing a control used to set the theme (color mode) used for the Earth application.",g8:"Summary description describing a switch to turn on High Contrast used for the Earth application.",Ew:'Summary description for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preference for formatting degrees. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for "Decimal" and "Degrees, Minutes, Seconds".',uR:'Summary description for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred area unit. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for various area unit options, e.g. "square meters", "square feet", etc.',v1:'Summary description for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred distance unit. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for various distance unit options, e.g. "meters", "miles", etc.',rT:'Summary description for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred unit for slope. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for various area unit options, e.g. "degrees", "percent", etc.',G5:'Summary description for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred unit system. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for "meters and kilometers" and "feet and miles".',HY:"Summary description for a setting option in google earth that governs the overall fly animation speed for camera.",as:"Summary description for a setting option that allow user to choose the type of animation to play for showing a place or region.",AM:"Summary description for a toggle button on the setting panel to enable or disable the fly animation. The fly animation is the animation that transitions the camera from the current view to the final view.",YU:"Switch to a graphical user interface optimized for larger screen size with keyboard and mouse.",Qy:"Switch to a graphical user interface optimized for mobile devices with touch input.",KG:"SystemChrome.setApplicationSwitcherDescription",xU:"Table header for a column showing the storage used of Earth documents.",Wn:"Table header for a values in a table that represent the minimum area of a building unit.",he:"Table header for a values in a table that represent the occupancy of a building unit. For example, a one bedroom building unit may have an occupancy of 1.",x5:"Table header for the percentage for a unit mix. For example, a building may have 10% one bedroom units. This table column represents the 10% value.",Vy:"Table row header for basement parking (e.g. underground parking garages) for the parking metrics table in the design details pabel.",PP:"Table row header for the materials used emissions summary table. This includes data about the materials used in construction and their associated emissions.",QY:"Table row header for the mechanical design details table. This includes data about the space within a building that is used for mechanical equipment, such as air conditioning, ventilation, or heating units.",es:"Targets refers to the target value of the gross floor area. Since the value is a target, it is what the designs will aim to have as the actual gross floor area value.",pM:"Text (and tooltip) for a button that allows a user to start measuring a new distance.",Np:"Text (and tooltip) for a button that allows a user to start the design tool input process again.",hP:"Text and tooltip text for a button that lets the user add new building use types to their designs. Use types refer to how the building will be used (e.g. for residential or commercial purposes).",WO:"Text below the Parking ratios section in the parking tab in the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. Parking ratios refers to the number of spots per building use type (e.g. for my residential building, I want 1 parking spot per 100 sq m).",IH:"Text box description for an optional text field where the user can send a message when requesting access to the owner of a project.",Dq:"Text describing the benefits of using the design tool for various kinds of real estate needs.",pD:"Text displayed when there are no Browser KML files to list and there is nothing left to do for the user to manage legacy KML files.",ju:"Text explaining how to use the 'placemark' drawing tool. Informing the user that they should click on the map to add the placemark.",IP:"Text explaining how to use the 'placemark' drawing tool. Informing the user that they should move the map to add the placemark.",hn:"Text explaining how to use the distance and area measurement tool. Informing the user that they should add points on the map to take a measurement.",oo:"Text explaining how to use the distance and area measurement tool. Informing the user that they should click on the map to add measurement points.",Ds:"Text explaining how to use the path and polygon drawing tool. Informing the user that they should add points in the path string or polygon boundary.",dA:"Text explaining how to use the path and polygon drawing tool. Informing the user that they should click on the map to add points in the path string or polygon boundary.",sa:"Text explaining the benefits of using the KML editor. This text is shown in a dialog that allows the user to open or create a new local KML file.",jg:"Text explaining the user they can move around the map, and enter Street View at the current center of the map.",NN:"Text explaining to the user that they should choose a design project type, then continue to select their site.",oZ:"Text for a Toast or Snackbar that informs the user that the 3D Buildings option is disabled while the Historical Imagery feature is active.",Ed:"Text for a Toast or Snackbar that informs the user that the 3D Buildings option is disabled while the Timelapse feature is active.",l6:"Text for a badge indicating that the current document is a local KML file.",De:"Text for a button that copies the current URL.",A:"Text for a button that creates a site analysis layer. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",El:"Text for a button that creates and opens a new local KML file. This button is shown in the KML editor dialog.",Em:"Text for a button that lets the user draw lines or shapes on the map.",Et:"Text for a button that opens a dialog to select a local KML file from the device. This button is shown in the KML editor dialog.",yl:"Text for a button that sends a request for access to a project.",PY:"Text for a button to group designs by date when viewing a list of designs.",D8:"Text for a button to reset the current compass heading to true north (i.e. heading 0).",U2:"Text for a checkbox in a survey about an Earth user's work or role. The checkbox controls whether the user opt-ins to receiving announcements about product and feature updates in Google Earth in the future.",hm:"Text for a checkbox in a survey about an Earth user's work or role. The checkbox controls whether the user opts in to market research, user studies, and feature pilots in Google Earth in the future.",ka:"Text for a checkbox in a survey about the geographic scope that an Earth user is interested in, for example: local, state, national, global.",Ap:"Text for a label for the imagery dates in the current view, shown in the data attribution dialog.",_0:"Text for a label for the list of map data providers, shown in the data attribution dialog.",TE:"Text for a label that notes that the current view shows imagery with unknown or unspecified imagery date information.",lb:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on an other, unspecified industry.",Fb:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the advertising / market research industry.",XT:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the agriculture industry.",FM:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the air quality/ pollution industry.",m3:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the architecture / urban design industry.",Fw:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the artificial intelligence and machine learning industry.",TK:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the asset valuation (insurance, banks, credit risk) industry.",hT:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the automotive industry.",Cu:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the battery / storage technology industry.",cq:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the business & professional services industry.",nh:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the city / urban / regional planning industry.",Ly:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the classroom or education industry.",D3:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the construction indu