to indicate that the user focuses on the tourism & leisure industry.",Mj:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the transportation infrastructure industry.",V2:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the transportation logistics (e.g., freight) industry.",b3:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the transportation planning industry.",U6:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the travel industry.",rA:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the trucking & transportation routing industry.",Hk:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the utilities planning or operations industry.",bI:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the area or industry of focus for an Earth user. This text is meant to indicate that the user focuses on the wind energy industry.",pC:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the user's primary use of Earth. This text is meant to indicate that the user uses Earth for academic research purposes.",R8:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the user's primary use of Earth. This text is meant to indicate that the user uses Earth for educational purposes as a student or teacher.",bv:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the user's primary use of Earth. This text is meant to indicate that the user uses Earth for government, public sector, or non-governmental organization (NGO) purposes.",pP:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the user's primary use of Earth. This text is meant to indicate that the user uses Earth for leisure or fun purposes.",l9:"Text for a radio button in a survey about the user's primary use of Earth. This text is meant to indicate that the user uses Earth for work or business purposes.",hU:"Text for a text button that allows a user to create more designs like this design using the same inputs by going through the design input tool again.",K3:"Text for a toast confirming the deletion of one or several features. The number of features being deleted is not known at the time of this toast.",gp:"Text for a toast that appears when the request to enter Street View failed because no Street View imagery is available at the point where the user dropped the pegman icon.",Ub:"Text for a tooltip around a button that, when hovered, will display a warning that only one site analysis layer can be generated at a given time.",zs:"Text for button in an option group to activate creating sites by drawing a polygon.",GK:"Text for button in an option group to activate creating sites by selecting tax lots.",iX:"Text for button in an option group to choose drawing a polygon.",hk:"Text for button in an option group to choose selecting a polygon.",Iq:"Text for button to show all designs when viewing a list of designs.",Pj:"Text for the button that clears search query.",Vw:"Text for the button that clears the current search results.",zr:"Text for the button that clears the current selected feature in a layer.",UG:"Text for the tooltip for a row header in the new build emissions summary metrics table in the design details panel, representing the distance travelled by automobiles. The number of automobiles is estimated from parking lots included in the design.",S4:"Text for the tooltip for the materials used row header in the emissions summary table. This includes data about the materials used in construction and their associated emissions.",FK:"Text for the tooltip of the design details table column header for a sustainability metrics table representing the emissions reduction that will result from the sustainability strategies selected for a design.",aI:"Text for the value proposition of KML files: specifically that the files are stored only on this device.",BC:"Text for the value proposition of using Google Drive for projects: specifically that these projects can be shared with other people, and with other devices.",CJ:"Text header to display before a formatted string containing a latitude / longitude coordinate.",pS:"Text header to display before a formatted string containing the date of a Street View image.",dx:"Text in a dialog that welcomes the user to the Google Earth 'Professional Advanced' plan. This text is shown above a list of features of the Professional Advanced plan.",TF:"Text in a dialog that welcomes the user to the Google Earth 'Professional' plan. This text is shown above a list of features of the Professional plan.",CZ:"Text in a menu item that clarifies which imperial units of measure are used for smaller area values and which ones are used for larger area values.",nr:"Text in a menu item that clarifies which imperial units of measure are used for smaller distance values and which ones are used for larger distance values.",nv:"Text in a menu item that clarifies which metric units of measure are used for smaller area values and which ones are used for larger area values.",rs:"Text in a menu item that clarifies which metric units of measure are used for smaller distance values and which ones are used for larger distance values.",gi:"Text in a menu item that clarifies which units of measurement are used for slope, where slope below 45 degrees will be shown as percent and slopes above 45 degrees will remain as degrees.",Bl:"Text in a tooltip for a building template card that indicates that the building template contains an invalid use type.",A7:"Text in an inline banner card on the buildings tab of the generate designs workflow. This text is shown if the user has enabled the basement parking toggle on the parking tab of the workflow. Basement parking refers to underground parking garages within buildings.",AQ:"Text in an inline banner card on the parking tab of the generate designs workflow that indicates that they can add parking garages as a building type when selecting building types for their site.",bQ:"Text in the Financials step of the create solar study workflow that describes the net metering preference field.",Re:"Text in the document view informing users that the document they are looking at is read-only.",Jj:"Text informing the user that they can share a URL or scan a QR code to open Google Earth on another device. Drawn before the URL and Qr code.",CF:"Text informing the user they must update Google Earth before continuing to use the product.",oV:"Text label shown in the import panel indicating that the import currently in progress can take up to 5 minutes.",bU:"Text label shown in the import panel while the user is importing a file into Google Earth, indicating that while the import is in progress, the user can leave the current page, but should not close the tab or window. If the user does close the tab or window, then their import operation will not succeed.",Ij:"Text label shown in the import panel while the user is importing a file into Google Earth, indicating that while the import is in progress, the user should not close the Earth app. If the user does close the app, then their import operation will not succeed.",SZ:"Text label shown with the date and time corresponding to when a layer was last updated.",ps:"Text label shown with the description of a data layer.",Lj:"Text label shown with the dropdown for changing the size of icons in a layer.",ea:"Text label shown with the list of data coverage regions for which data is available in a layer.",NP:"Text label shown with the list of data sources used in a layer.",Ex:"Text label shown with the list of terms of use restrictions for a layer. Example restriction: 'Because this layer contains some proprietary data, it cannot be exported as KML.'",iM:"Text label shown with the name of a selected feature.",B0:"Text label shown with the slider that controls the opacity of a selected layer.",LM:"Text next to a toggle that allows users to enable or disable quality of life metrics. When enabled, generated designs will include data on quality of life metrics such as sun hours, walkability, and more.",P6:'Text of a button allowing the user to bypass the process of choosing or creating a project and simply get to the main Google Earth experience.  "Earth" here should be considered a shortened version of "Google Earth", not the name of the planet.',xJ:"Text of a button allowing the user to create a new Earth Map Project on Google Drive.",UI:"Text of a button allowing the user to create a new local KML Earth project. Note: KML stands for Keyhole Markup Language. It should not be translated, unless the language has another abbreviation for KML.",mv:"Text of a button allowing the user to dismiss the welcome dialog and start using Earth.",LG:"Text of a button allowing the user to import a local KML file into an existing Earth project.",om:"Text of a button allowing the user to open the settings dialog in order to view their plan and billing information. Shown in the welcome dialog, when a user returns to the app after subscribing to an Earth plan.",QF:"Text of a button allowing the user to replace the contents of a feature that were authored by Google with their own description.",xg:"Text of a button displayed in the Data Table if there was a generic error while fetching or displaying data for the data table. Clicking it re-fetches the data.",rr:"Text of a button in the Filter tab of the inspector panel that is shown when a user selects a data layer. The button lets the user add a filter for a new attribute to the data layer.",EK:"Text of a button in the Filter tab of the inspector panel that is shown when a user selects a data layer. The button lets the user reset all filters to their default values.",uU:"Text of a button in the Style tab of the inspector panel that is shown when a user selects a data layer. The button lets the user reset all styles to their default values.",pc:"Text of a button in the left panel on the home screen. The button opens a dialog that allows the user to open or create a new local KML file stored on the user's device, as opposed to in the cloud",A_:"Text of a button prompting the user to refresh the app in order to enable their Google Earth Professional Advanced subscription.",aP:"Text of a button shown in a warning banner in a popup dialog, that the user presses to download all of the KML files displayed in that dialog.",mj:"Text of a button that allows a user to get more storage by upgrading their billing plan.",PE:"Text of a button that allows the user to create a new local KML file.",BR:"Text of a button that allows the user to create a new project in Google Drive.",Sx:"Text of a button that allows the user to create or open a new Drive project or KML file -- ideally a single word.",OS:"Text of a button that exits the Timelapse feature.",UL:"Text of a button that opens the Google Earth terms of service in a new window.",nS:'Text of a button that resets the transform of a 3D model back to their default (identity) values. Should be consistent with the translation of "modelTransform".',KX:"Text of a button that shows a dialog displaying files stored in browser storage; the button is displayed within a banner warning the user that their KML file stored in browser storage will no longer be accessible after a certain date.",AJ:"Text of a button that shows a dialog displaying files stored in browser storage; the button is displayed within a banner warning the user that their KML files stored in browser storage will no longer be accessible after a certain date.",nb:"Text of a button that, when clicked, will clear the saved camera view from a feature.",uP:'Text of a button that, when clicked, will save the current position and angle from which the user is looking at an object on the map and use that whenever the object is flown to. "Capture" here is used in the same sense as it might be to describe taking a photograph of something. To prevent confusion, please avoid using the same word that you would use to describe saving a file on a computer.',Fo:"Text of a dialog that lets the user type or paste a URL to add media to a feature",Yh:"Text of a guiding message that explains to the user what to do in the create a site step.",i2:'Text of a label allowing the user to specify the amount of tilt associated with a 3D model. Note that "Tilt" here is a noun meaning "the degree to which something is tilted".',oR:'Text of a label allowing the user to specify the amount of tilt associated with a camera position. Note that "Tilt" here is a noun meaning "the degree to which something is tilted".',uq:'Text of a label allowing the user to specify the heading associated with a camera position. Heading is similar to "direction", but is a numeric quantity where 0 is due north, 180 is south, etc. Not to be confused with "bearing", which is direction relative to an object.',uH:'Text of a label allowing the user to specify the heading associated with a model. Heading is similar to "direction", but is a numeric quantity where 0 is due north, 180 is south, etc. Not to be confused with "bearing", which is direction relative to an object.',C5:"Text of a label allowing the user to specify the range associated with a camera position. The range is the distance between the camera and the point that the camera is focused on.",uW:"Text of a label describing a control used to set the theme (color mode) used for the Earth application.",iN:"Text of a label describing a switch to turn on High Contrast used for the Earth application.",al:"Text of a label informing the user that the information for the feature they are currently editing was provided by Google, and thus cannot be edited without being replaced entirely.  Ideally this should be relatively brief, since it is intended to fit on one line within a small card.",Cm:"Text of a link in the Error Guide to copy the full error log to the clipboard.",W:"Text of a link that brings the user to a Help Center article explaining the feature the link is associated with.",iP:"Text of a menu dropdown to display all steps in a workflow that a user can navigate to.",AB:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to collapse a folder to show all of its internal features.",Q_:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to collapse the parent folder of all selected features",ks:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to delete all of the features (placemarks, etc.) that are currently selected.",Ba:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to expand a folder to show all of its internal features.",kQ:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to hide on the map all of the features (placemarks, etc.) that are currently selected.",YM:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to show on the map all of the features (placemarks, etc.) that are currently selected.",fQ:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to specify that a feature on the map should be displayed at a certain altitude above the ground beneath it (as opposed to an altitude above sea level or directly on the ground).",pq:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to specify that a feature on the map should be displayed at a certain altitude above the sea floor beneath it (as opposed to an altitude above sea level or directly on the sea floor).",eb:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to specify that a feature on the map should be displayed at a certain altitude above the surface model.",EV:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to specify that a feature on the map should be displayed at a certain altitude relative to sea level (as opposed to an altitude above the ground or sea floor below the feature).",sE:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to specify that a feature on the map should be displayed directly on the ground beneath it (as opposed to suspended in the air).",zt:"Text of a menu item allowing the user to specify that a feature on the map should be displayed directly on the sea floor beneath it (as opposed to suspended in the air or floating in the ocean).",pV:"Text of a menu item in the Filter tab of the inspector panel that is shown when a user selects a data layer. The menu item lets the user delete the filter for a single data layer attribute.",SI:"Text of a menu item in the Filter tab of the inspector panel that is shown when a user selects a data layer. The menu item lets the user reset the filter for a single data layer attribute to its default values.",pA:"Text of a menu item that allows the user to paste what is currently on their clipboard into a folder.",Wh:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should both fly to that feature and show an info card containing information about the feature.",Gx:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should both fly to that feature and show an info card containing information about the feature. This text should be as brief as possible, ideally no more than five words.",C0:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should ensure that the feature is invisible on the globe.",LB:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should ensure that the feature is invisible on the globe. This text should be as brief as possible, ideally no more than five words.",NY:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should ensure that the feature is visible on the globe.",u9:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should ensure that the feature is visible on the globe. This text should be as brief as possible, ideally no more than five words.",Kw:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should fly to that feature.",QZ:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should fly to that feature. This text should be as brief as possible, ideally no more than five words.",hF:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should show an info card containing information about that feature.",g2:"Text of a menu item that the user can select to indicate that when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked, Google Earth should show an info card containing information about that feature. This text should be as brief as possible, ideally no more than five words.",fy:"Text of a paragraph explaining to the user that the information for the feature they are currently editing was provided by Google, and thus cannot be edited without being replaced entirely.  This can be as long as necessary, as it will wrap to multiple lines.",OG:"Text of a promo card that promotes and describes the use of bulk editing for features.",hl:"Text of a promo card that promotes and describes the use of undo/redo when editing features.",YF:"Text of a segmented button that switches from the Historical Imagery feature to the Timelapse feature.",rx:"Text of a segmented button that switches from the Timelapse feature to the Historical Imagery feature.",Pt:"Text of a title that encourages the user to start create a site by selecting a tax lot or draw a shape.",Bp:"Text of a toast informing the user that the Google Drive app is not installed and that the Drive picker cannot be opened.",Xn:"Text of a toast informing the user that the document could not load from the Google Drive app for an unknown reason.",xz:"Text of a toast telling the user how to start a slideshow after slides have been generated.",HJ:"Text of a toast that lets the user know that the paste operation failed because clipboard access was denied by the system.",Xi:"Text of a toast that lets the user know that the paste operation failed because they attempted to paste an unsupported data type into the project.",e0:"Text of a toast that lets the user know that the paste operation failed because they attempted to paste into a read-only folder.",o5:"Text of a tooltip for a button that lets the user enter Google Street View at a pre-specified latitude and longitude.",iC:"Text of a tooltip that describes a new feature.  Due to technical limitations, this will always appear before the feature description in local reading order.",pb:"Text of an error message shown when the user has entered an invalid country or region name.",W9:"Text of an introduction title for an information panel that encourages the user to search for a specific location or zoom in closer in the map to start create a site for design and development.",Qg:"Text of an introduction title for an information panel that encourages the user to search for a specific location or zoom out from the map to start create a site for design and development.",v9:"Text of label or tooltip for a button that the user can still press to add the associated KML file to a map project in the cloud. The text of the button indicates that the associated project has already been added to a project.",PG:"Text of label or tooltip for a button that the user pressed to download the associated KML file to their device; the button text changes from 'Download' to 'Downloaded' after the button is pressed for the first time.",Sm:"Text of label or tooltip for a button that the user presses to add the associated KML file to a map project in the cloud.",Gd:"Text of label or tooltip for a button that the user presses to download the associated KML file to their device.",m7:"Text of label or tooltip for a buttonthat indicates that the associated project is currently being added to a project.",U:"Text of the button to close and dismiss a promotion card for a new Earth feature, like the new Earth Home screen explore Earth button or onboarding info panel for design generation.",wy:"Text of the button to try a new Earth feature, like the new Earth Home screen explore Earth button or onboarding info panel for design generation.",wV:"Text of the card body text to inform the user that their site exceeds the maximum site area limit in the design inputs view.",TM:"Text of the card body text to inform the user that their site exceeds the maximum site area limit in the design inputs view. An upgrade is possible as the user's active license does not have the highest max site area capability.",wR:"Text of the card body text to inform the user that their site exceeds the maximum site area limit in the design inputs view. An upgraded plan is available as the user has another license with a higher max site area capability.",Wj:"Text of the card body text to inform the user that their site exceeds the maximum site area limit in the design inputs view. No upgrade is possible as the user's active plan already has the highest max site area capability.",i1:"Text of the card body text to inform the user to they have reached the acre limit in their current plan. An upgrade is possible as the user is not in the Professional Advanced plan.",VV:"Text of the card body text to inform the user to they have reached the design limit in their current plan. An upgrade is not possible as the user is in the Professional Advanced plan.",p7:"Text of the card body text to inform the user to they have reached the design limit in their current plan. An upgrade is possible as the user has a project in a higher Earth plan.",SJ:"Text of the card body text to inform the user to they have reached the design limit in their current plan. An upgrade is possible as the user is not in the Professional Advanced plan.",Ch:"Text of the card body text to inform the user to they have reached the maximum site area limit in the site selection view. No upgrade is possible as the user is already in the Professional Advanced plan.",lQ:"Text of the card body text to inform the user to they have reached the maximum site area limit in their current plan. An upgrade is possible as the user has a project in a higher Earth plan.",It:"Text of the promotion card body for the new Street View timeline feature, when the feature is disabled due to lack of data.",DH:"Text of the promotion card body for the new Street View timeline feature.",vh:"Text of the promotion card body for the request access button",pl:"Text of the promotion card body text to invite the user to select the project with a higher Earth plan to use tax lot site selection.",xF:"Text of the promotion card body text to invite the user to upgrade to Earth 'Professional' or 'Professional Advanced' plan in the site selection view if they want to use tax lot site selection.",IU:"Text of the promotion card for the Earth logo, which encourages the user to click on the logo to find and manage their Earth projects.",yS:"Text of the small promotional card for adding sources (images, kml files, etc.) to a Earth Mate (Earth AI assistant) request.",F7:'Text on a button in a view that promotes the Earth AI assistant. Pressing the button creates a map and opens the Earth AI assistant. "Ask" here is a reference to the feature name "Ask Google Earth" (AI assistant chat bot) and should be translated consistently with how that term is translated.',b9:"Text on a button that allows the user to create an empty project in Google Earth.",Xl:'Text on a button that creates an empty project in Google Earth before opening the Earth AI assistant. "Prompting" refers to the process of sending text (questions, commands, etc.) to the AI assistant to generate a response. This is a longer version of [earthMateBrowseModeCreateProject]',WY:"Text on a button that opens a link to manage the user's Google One AI plan.",mQ:"Text on a menu item for starting a new conversation thread with the Earth AI assistant.",nK:"Text on a tooltip of an error card explaining that the polygon the user has drawn has an area that is too large for Earth to generate designs for.",n6:"Text on a tooltip of an error card explaining that the polygon the user has drawn has an area that is too small for Earth to generate designs for.",OM:"Text on a tooltip of an error card explaining that the polygon the user has drawn has too many points in it for Earth to generate designs for.",xn:"Text on a tooltip of an error card explaining that the polygon the user has drawn is self-intersected and cannot be used to generate designs.",Te:"Text showing the user that the filters they edited for a data layer have been automatically saved to the current project on Google Drive.",Cx:"Text showing the user that the styles they edited for a data layer have been automatically saved to the current project on Google Drive.",Zi:"Text shown as a footnote to the area description field, explaining that the area description is generated by AI.",Xw:"Text shown in a button that opens a data table showing individual rows of data for features in a data layer.",BD:"Text shown in a button that switches the user to a 2D view.",qE:"Text shown in a card indicating that a layer is removed and will no longer be supported in the Earth product.",nP:"Text shown in a card indicating that the document asset layer is associated with a different map and cannot be viewed.",cI:"Text shown in a card indicating that the selected layer is unavailable at the moment and cannot be viewed.",TZ:"Text shown in a card indicating that the user does not have the correct billing plan and that an upgrade is needed.",NZ:"Text shown in a dialog asking the user to confirm that they want to remove a project that had been shared with them on Google Drive. Please make sure to use https: links.",Ka:"Text shown in a dialog asking the user to select as many options as they like in a survey.",fq:"Text shown in a dialog that prompts the user to open their settings to activate an upgrade to their plan that will allow them to filter data layers by area.",oK:"Text shown in a dialog that prompts the user to open their settings to activate an upgrade to their plan that will allow them to use additional data layers.",h2:"Text shown in a dialog that prompts the user to open their settings to activate an upgrade to their plan that will allow them to view the data layer.",Jw:"Text shown in a dialog when no data layers are available to be added to the current project.",NV:"Text shown in a snackbar to alert the user that the Earth app has stopped.",_1:"Text shown in a table row header for a metric representing the operational energy offset by solar panels for a given design. This represents the estimated energy used by buildings in this design.",cY:"Text shown in a table row header for a metric representing the operational energy usage for a given design.",tE:"Text shown in a toast that appears when a project is deleted.",a3:"Text shown in a toast to alert the user that there is nothing to paste.",Pn:"Text shown in a toast to alert the user to an error condition.",dj:"Text shown in the 'about' section of the settings indicating the user is receiving Dogfood experiment flags.",cm:"Text shown in the 'about' section of the settings indicating the user is receiving Fishfood experiment flags.",rY:"Text shown in the 'about' section of the settings indicating the user is receiving Trusted Tester experiment flags.",bK:"Text shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window when the user does not have a project open. This message is followed by a text button 'Open a map project'. \"Prompting\" refers to the process of sending text (questions, commands, etc.) to the AI assistant to generate a response.",_O:"Text shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window while waiting for a response from the server.",NQ:"Text shown in the area filter panel when the user's active plan does not have the ability to create an area filter.",_P:'Text shown in the data attribution dialog to indicate that the default zoning data shown in the create design input flow is from the Zoneomics dataset. Zoneomics is the name of a third party company that provides zoning data. Zone refers to zoning laws that indicate where buildings can be built. "-omics" is a suffix used to describe the study of something.',cG:"Text shown in the inspector panel when the user selects a data layer. This text describes how one may interact with the layer.",ZU:"Text shown in the middle of the screen to inform users that they can drop the files they are currently dragging into Earth.",S:"Text shown in the place of a metric value when there is no data available.",_U:"Text shown in the place of any missing design name when there is no data available when viewing generated designs in the design viewer view.",gR:"Text shown in the request access dialog indicating the user is signed in as the given email address.",jp:"Text shown in the section of the inspector panel for editing styles of labels within a layer.",cW:"Text shown in the section of the inspector panel for editing styles of paths within a layer.",s0:"Text shown in the section of the inspector panel for editing styles of points within a layer.",Eu:"Text shown in the section of the inspector panel for editing styles of polygons within a layer.",vp:"Text shown in the side panel along side a loading spinner while an Earth map is being created. Once the creation is complete, the text and spinner are hidden and options to add features to the map are shown.",gh:"Text shown in the toolbar when the user activates Street View coverage mode to select a Street View location.",Ct:"Text shown in the tooltip for a table row header for a metric representing the operational energy offset by solar panels for a given design. This represents the estimated energy used by buildings in this design.",PJ:"Text shown in the tooltip for a table row header for a metric representing the operational energy usage for a given design.",X:"Text shown on buttons allowing the user to acknowledge a dialog.",mk:"Text shown to indicate that design generation is blocked due to invalid inputs.",df:"Text shown to indicate that design generation is temporarily unavailable.",QE:"Text that describes the quality of life metrics. When enabled, generated built environment designs will include data on sun hours, walkability, daylight access, and views to parks and/or water.",tW:"Text that informs the user about the Shift and Control keyboard shortcuts for controlling the camera. Shift drag will tilt and rotate the view. Control drag will look around.",B9:"Text that informs the user that their changes in a KML project are not auto-saved.",tk:"Text that is shown in the Filter tab of the inspector panel when a user selects a data layer. The text is shown after a dropdown menu containing the name of the filter, and before a list of the currently selected options for the filter.",m0:"Text that is shown in the Filter tab of the inspector panel when a user selects a data layer. The text is shown after a dropdown menu containing the name of the filter, and before a range slider for the filter, which allows the user to select a min and max value for the filter.",jq:"Text that is shown in the Filter tab of the inspector panel when a user selects a data layer. The text is shown between the min and max values for a range filter, indicating that the filter will return data that is between those values.",Ga:"Text to promote the create more button. This prompts users to change the inputs or information that they have entered to create a previous building development or solar panel design so that they can create more designs like this one.",Av:"Text to prompt users to activate their upgraded plan to create a contour layer. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",mr:"Text to prompt users to activate their upgraded plan to create a cut and fill layer. Cut and fill analysis is a process that measures the volume of earth material that needs to be moved to create a level area of land.",qI:"Text to prompt users to activate their upgraded plan to create a slope layer. Slope refers to the steepness of the terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",EQ:"Text to prompt users to activate their upgraded plan to create an aspect layer. Aspect is the direction that a slope faces. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",Vr:"Text to prompt users to activate their upgraded plan to use a larger site or area for their analysis. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",pd:"Text to prompt users to upgrade their plan to create a contour layer. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",tS:"Text to prompt users to upgrade their plan to create a cut and fill layer. Cut and fill analysis is a process that measures the volume of earth material that needs to be moved to create a level area of land.",UC:"Text to prompt users to upgrade their plan to create a slope layer. Slope refers to the steepness of the terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",sH:"Text to prompt users to upgrade their plan to create an aspect layer. Aspect is the direction that a slope faces. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",Tk:"Text to show error in a small pop up toast at the bottom of the screen",Aa:"Text used as a placeholder inviting the user to provide a description for a project. This is shown in the document view panel only if the project doesn't have a description.",P9:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as FAR values (floor area ratio). This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "FAR". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',R:"Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as angles measured in degrees. This should be translated as the degree symbol (\xb0) unless that would not be understood. For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.",kx:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in acres. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "ac". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',pL:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in hectares. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "ha". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',gw:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in square feet. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "ft\xb2". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',bZ:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in square kilometers. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "km\xb2". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',on:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in square miles. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "mi\xb2". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',En:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in square miles. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "m\xb2". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',OF:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in square nautical miles. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "NM\xb2". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',xM:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as areas measured in square yards. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "yd\xb2". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',Bs:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in centimeters. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "cm". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',Nc:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in feet. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "ft". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',eB:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in inches. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "in". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',VL:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in kilometers. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "km". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',c:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in meters. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "m". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',Bo:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in miles. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "mi". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',Qr:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in nautical miles. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "NM". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',sC:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in smoots. A smoot is an obscure unit of measurement whose name is derived from the name of a person, Oliver R. Smoot. It can therefore generally be transliterated directly into your language\'s alphabet or syllabary. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "mi". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',YG:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as distances measured in yards. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "yd". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',_W:'Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as percentages. Should only be used for text field suffixes, not for formatting numbers as percentages. This should be short, preferably an abbreviation such as "%". For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.',d2:"Text used as a suffix for text fields whose inputs are interpreted as sizes measured in pixels. For technical reasons this must be a suffix, and cannot be made to agree with the number to which it applies. Please file a bug if this makes translation impossible.",Es:"Text used to inform users that generation of their Built Environment designs is in progress. This is shown as a badge on the thumbnail image in the Design Viewer panel, after the user has submitted a set of inputs to generate designs.",pn:"Text used to inform users that their Built Environment designs are being generated. This is shown on the Design Viewer panel, after the user has submitted a set of inputs to generate designs.",PW:"TextInputClient.updateEditingStateWithDeltas",CY:"TextInputClient.updateEditingStateWithTag",Lw:"That action couldn\u2019t be performed right now, but we\u2019ll keep trying",cP:"The GeoJSON file is missing a valid 'features' array.",cQ:"The GeoJSON file must contain a 'type' field that has a string value.",Ye:"The GeoJSON file must contain a 'type' field.",UQ:"The GeoJSON file must contain a FeatureCollection object.",bi:"The Google Cloud project you select is only used to manage your plan and unrelated to any projects you create in Google Earth.",Hb:"The KMZ file could not be opened. Ensure the file is a valid KMZ file and try again.",Qd:"The KMZ file references a file that is not included in the KMZ. Ensure all files referenced by the KMZ are included in the archive and try again.",i_:"The Screen Readerlong press hint for a button that pans the map up for a long distance.",j5:"The Screen Readerlong press hint for a button that rotates the map for a long distance.",du:"The Screen Readerlong press hint for a button that tilts the map for a long distance.",FB:"The Timelapse feature is now available from the Basemap Settings menu.",Id:"The ZIP file could not be opened. Ensure the file is a valid ZIP file and try again.",MQ:"The accessibility label of a horizontal list of images that can be expanded.",mR:"The accessilbity label to be read for the Navigation Controls.",Rh:"The amount the utility will charge per unit in kilowatt-hours of electricity consumed.",h9:"The annual distance traveled by automobiles within a site",RM:"The annual rate of increase of electricity rate.",cb:"The annual rate of increase of the PPA price.",nY:"The annual rate of increase of the lease rate.",yi:"The building templates you select will generate buildings that vary in size and configuration based on your specifications. You will be able to customize the stack order and geometry settings for each type after you add them.",dY:"The content below is controlled by the author of this project. For your safety, do not enter passwords or other personal information.",pY:"The data failed to load. If this continues, please report the issue.",hI:"The data in the clipboard cannot be pasted into the selected folder because it is view-only.",b0:"The daylight access quality of life metric. This text shows up in a list below the option to enable the quality of life metrics. When enabled, generated designs will include data quality of life metrics including daylight access, which shows how much daylight a building receives.",wp:"The default name of a 3D model that the user creates.",Fv:"The default name of a Street View photo panorama that the user wishes to save to their project.",z_:"The default name of a feature that doesn't have a name, if the feature is of an uncommon type.",dh:"The default name of a folder that the user creates.",re:"The default name of a fullscreen slide that the user creates.",gD:"The default name of a layer that the user creates.",H3:"The default name of a measurement that the user creates.",Eh:"The default name of a path that the user creates.",X2:"The default name of a point placemark that the user creates.",p4:"The default name of a polygon that the user creates.",mU:"The description for a settings list that will let the user choose one of three options for dark mode settings.",UW:"The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included only if more than 1 sustainability strategy is not turned on.",nw:"The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included only if no sustainability strategies have been applied to a design.",YV:"The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is shown for all designs. This indicates to users the impact numbers (e.g. carbon emissions reduction percentages, amount tCO2e emissions reductions) are calculateed by comparing the design without any sustainability strategies applied to the design (known as the baseline) with sustainability strategies applied.",iT:"The description for the settings option to enable on-screen centered drawing tools, as opposed to tools that follow the mouse pointer on the screen.",pW:"The distance from the exterior facade to the core or corridor for this group of floors. Default values are based on dimensions from common building types in North American markets.",uZ:"The document could not be parsed due to a formatting error. Please double-check the file structure, then try importing again.",Ma:"The document has reached the maximum number of features and no more feature can be added",L2:"The document is getting close to the limit of features",s3:"The element contains a hotspot with invalid xunits. Defaulting to pixels.",OA:"The element contains a hotspot with invalid yunits. Defaulting to pixels.",PT:"The element contains an unsupported display mode.",yx:"The element has an attribute missing a schema reference. Please ensure all attributes reference a valid schema ID.",Jh:"The estimated energy offset by building solar in this design",kW:"The estimated energy used by buildings in this design",rH:"The feature could not be imported due to an unknown error.",M_:"The feature has a line that does not have at least two unique coordinates and was placed at 0,0.",IX:"The feature has a linear ring that does not have at least three unique coordinates to form a closed polygon and was placed at 0,0.",EY:"The feature has a linear ring that does not have matching first and last coordinates to form a closed polygon and was placed at 0,0.",dG:"The feature has a point missing the latitude coordinate and was placed at 0,0.",Ac:"The feature has a point missing the longitude coordinate and was placed at 0,0.",so:"The feature has a polygon that is missing an outer boundary and was placed at 0,0.",a2:"The file must contain a <kml> tag as the first element after the XML declaration, if present. Add or move the <kml> tag to the correct position and try again.",Af:"The financial model for solar studies evaluates two financing options for solar systems: buying and leasing. The financial metrics were modeled with the adjusted assumptions during study setup and default values from collected data.",yy:"The header for the total emissions row in the emissions summary table. This represents the sum of all embodied carbon emissions and ten years of operational and transportation emissions.",vO:"The header/title of the part of the basemap styles form where additional layers such as photos, gridlines, and animated clouds can be selected.",iU:"The hint (placeholder) text for a dropdown menu asking the user to select a feature in the current project to add a link to.",xN:"The label for Screen Readers to notify the user that they are focusing the Search Bar group.",RI:"The label for Screen Readers to notify the user they are on the design thumbnail.",ne:"The label for a button that deletes the currently viewed layer.",F8:"The label for a button that opens a modal with the different billing plans available.",aY:"The label for a column in a data table that shows the date or time at which a project that the user might choose to load in Google Earth was accessed by them.",gq:"The label for a column in a data table that shows the date or time at which a project that the user might choose to load in Google Earth was modified by someone.",St:"The label for a column in a data table that shows the name (or title) of a project that the user might choose to load in Google Earth.",Lq:"The label for a column in a data table that shows the name and image of the person who owns a project that the user might choose to load in Google Earth.",z6:'The label for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preference for formatting degrees. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for "Decimal" and "Degrees, Minutes, Seconds".',b5:'The label for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred area unit. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for various area unit options, e.g. "square meters", "square feet", etc.',Io:'The label for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred distance unit. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for various distance unit options, e.g. "meters", "miles", etc.',Ip:'The label for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred unit for slope. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for various area unit options, e.g. "degrees", "percent", etc.',Ck:'The label for a dropdown menu allowing the user to select their preferred unit system. Options in the menu will be the localized strings for "meters and kilometers" and "feet and miles".',Bm:"The label for a dropdown menu that allows the user to chose the visual quality of the 3D display.",Qs:"The label for a settings switch that will let the user enable darkmode, or lightmode if the option is disabled.",XW:"The label for a tooltip on an icon that indicates that a project it's associated with is shared using a link (as opposed to shared only with specific people).",jl:"The label for a tooltip on an icon that indicates that a project it's associated with is shared with specific people.  The current user may or may not be the one who shared the project.",V3:"The label for an app theme setting that tells the app to always use dark mode.",EJ:"The label for an app theme setting that tells the app to always use light mode.",s2:"The label for an app theme setting that tells the app to use the system's theme.",wQ:"The label for an undo button to inform the users that the button will undo their last action.",o7:"The label for the toolbar that appears at the top of the design details to be read by screen readers.",x9:"The label of a radio button.  When the radio button is selected, it indicates that the user wants to add a link (hyperlink) to a URL, as opposed to a link to a feature.",t9:"The label of a radio button.  When the radio button is selected, it indicates that the user wants to add a link (hyperlink) to a feature in the current project, as opposed to a link to a URL.",Kc:"The label of a section in a dialog that lets the user choose an action to perform when a link (hyperlink) to a feature is clicked. This serves as a clause in an implied sentence, the second half of which is determined by the text of a dropdown menu just below this label.",VS:"The label of a text field allowing the user to type the URL they want to add a link (hyperlink) to. The link will be inserted into the rich text editor for the current feature's description.",hy:"The label on the input field used to select values in a dropdown menu.",qv:"The last attempt to add this file to a project failed.",G8:"The lifetime (25 year) savings discounted to today's value.",qw:"The maximum allowed Building Coverage Ratio for each block in the parcel, defined as the percentage of the block's land area that is covered by buildings.",rQ:"The maximum allowed Floor Area Ratio for each block in the parcel. This limits the total GFA.",aw:"The message on the snackbar shown when the user tries to edit too many features at once.",RB:"The minimum and maximum number of floors for this group. The actual number of generated floors will vary in this range to meet your development program target GFAs. Default values are based on common building types in North American markets.",DK:"The minimum required Open Space Ratio for each block in this parcel, defined as the percentage of the block's land area that is preserved as open space.",iG:"The monthly cost to lease solar panels for building roofs from a solar company through a regular leasing contract.",ao:"The monthly cost to lease solar panels for parking lots from a solar company through a regular leasing contract.",jV:"The name of a data column/attribute label showing the GPS accuracy of the point represented by the feature, with units of meters.",GA:"The name of the company.  This is shown alone as a text hint for the Google logo.",TI:"The name of the menu bar to be read by Screen Readers.",Bi:"The name of the product.  This is only rarely localized; leave untranslated unless you're certain.",YZ:"The per-kilowatt-hour price for using the energy generated from the solar panels through a PPA (Power Purchase Agreement).",CA:"The percentage difference between rentable area and usable area. Default values are based on common building types in North American markets.",Lo:"The percentage of the net system cost (with cost-based incentives applied) that you would like to finance with a loan.",bg:"The plan name of the Google One AI Plus plan.",ED:"The plan name of the Google One AI Pro plan.",eJ:"The plan name of the Google One AI Ultra plan.",DC:"The program for this group of floors. Can be one or more use types in the same class, based on your development program. Default values are based on dimensions from common building types in North American markets.",e5:"The required distance that a development must be setback from a front lot line. Max 20ft/6.096m.",n2:"The required distance that a development must be setback from a rear lot line. Max 20ft/6.096m.",zA:"The required distance that a development must be setback from a side lot line. Max 20ft/6.096m.",hC:"The schema contains a field missing a name. Please provide a name.",eA:"The semantics label for the button that opens a dropdown-like menu to show all the steps in a workflow for a user to select from.",Uc:"The short product name for the Google Timelapse feature described at https://blog.google/products/earth/new-imagery-google-earth-timelapse-videos/.",EM:"The sun hours quality of life metric. This text shows up in a list below the option to enable the quality of life metrics. When enabled, generated designs will include data quality of life metrics including sun hours, which shows how many hours of sunlight a building receives.",D0:"The table header for the unit mix column. The unit mix refers to the percentage of different types of residential units in a building. For example, a building may have 10% one bedroom units, 40% two bedroom units, and 50% three bedroom units.",gX:"The target document ACL does not allow the import.",MN:"The target document has reached the maximum number of features.",hW:"The target document or folder does not exist.",Pv:"The text for a button that triggers Street View in the selected location.",OD:"The text for a setting shown in the Settings view that if activated, will display an on-screen navigation controls view.",Tr:"The text of a tooltip for a button in Google Earth that tilts the view from perspective 3D to top-down 2D.",A6:"The text of a tooltip for a button in Google Earth that tilts the view from top-down 2D to perspective 3D.",fW:"The text shown to a user when they attempt to add a URL to a feature that does not link to an image.",Cq:"The text used for the toast that promotes the 3D imagery toggle.",Cz:"The text used for the tooltip on the thumb down feedback button.",nV:"The text used for the tooltip on the thumb up feedback button.",Cs:"The title at the top of the navigation controls view.",_8:"The title for a summary table in the Design details panel. This is used for various new build and solar metrics tables (e.g. Program, Solar Financials).",vc:"The title for on-screen navigation controls settings option.",mL:"The title for the collapsable category for Accessibility found in the Settings dialog.",uQ:"The title for the settings option to enable on-screen centered drawing tools, as opposed to tools that follow the mouse pointer on the screen.",Yo:"The title of a dialog allowing the user to add a link (hyperlink) to a URL or to another feature in the current project. The link will be inserted into the rich text editor for the current feature's description.",EN:"The title of a dialog allowing the user to add building use types to their designs.",TN:"The title of a dialog allowing the user to edit a building type's configuration.",BI:"The title of the default Earth map, to which features will be added if the user has not created a map for them to go in.  Shown in the My places panel tree view.  Translate on a best-effort basis, and try to preserve the sense that this is an informal, possibly temporary place for things to go.",UU:"The title of the default Google Earth site study, where users can generate potential designs with changes to the built environment.",rg:"The title to use for a project that has been recovered from local disk, memory, or browser storage after an error has occurred, e.g. clearing browswer cache. For recovered projects the original name will be lost.",go:"The tooltip explaining the user that if they tap on the image, the image carousel will be enlarged on the screen.",Y0:"The tooltip for a button that pans the map down for a short distance.",ko:"The tooltip for a button that pans the map to the left for a short distance.",Ue:"The tooltip for a button that pans the map to the right for a short distance.",x_:"The tooltip for a button that pans the map up for a short distance.",lg:"The tooltip for a button that rotates the map clockwise.",gH:"The tooltip for a button that tilts the map down for a short distance.",s7:"The tooltip for a button that tilts the map up for a short distance.",Qe:"The tooltip for the use type dropdown selector in the basement section of the building editor tab. Basement floors can only be used for parking.",Tm:"The tooltip for the use type dropdown selector in the building editor tab. A use type describes the floor's intended usage such as being used for residential, office, or retail space.",OV:"The tooltip text for a button that will zoom in the view on map when user tap on it.",SC:"The tooltip text for a button that will zoom out the view on map when user tap on it.",cX:"The total carbon associated with the materials used for buildings in this design",WS:"The total investments or payments required after cost based incentives are applied. (payments of cash, loan + interest, lease or PPA)",NX:"The total per-watt cost of installing solar panels on a building roof, including the cost of the panels, labor cost, other soft costs, etc.",RS:"The total per-watt cost of installing solar panels on a parking lot, including the cost of the panels, labor cost, other soft costs, etc.",py:"The total projected baseline emissions for the design over the next 10 years. This includes embodied carbon emissions, and 10 years of operational and transportation emissions.",UJ:"The type of data in the clipboard cannot be pasted directly into an Earth project.",ta:"The unit shown for the price of the Earth premium plan. This refers to a price that is per user per month in USD.",B8:"The vertical distance between the finished floor surface of one level and the finished floor surface of the level above. Default values are based on dimensions from common building types in North American markets.",hb:"The views quality of life metric. This text shows up in a list below the option to enable the quality of life metrics. When enabled, generated designs will include data quality of life metrics including views, which scores buildings based on things like views to parks/water.",Qf:"The visibility of 3D Buildings can be toggled in the basemap panel.",_d:"The walkability quality of life metric. This text shows up in a list below the option to enable the quality of life metrics. When enabled, generated designs will include data quality of life metrics including walkability, which shows how walkable a building is to common attractions like parks and restaurants.",aL:"The width of the double-loaded corridor for this group of floors. Default values are based on dimensions from common building types in North American markets.",Mi:"The year used to generate the layer. Your sample points apply to that year's map",vL:"There was a problem trying to load FontManifest.json",qR:"These assumptions will be used to calculate the net cash flow for leasing solar panels over the typical lifespan.",jn:"These assumptions will be used to calculate the net cash flow for owning solar panels over the typical lifespan.",Nr:"These assumptions will be used to calculate the total cost of the solar project and total electricity costs and savings with and without solar installation.",qV:"This YouTube video has already been added to this feature.",Zv:"This determines how much parking will be generated.",Is:"This feature cannot be added because the project's feature count limit has been reached.",hq:"This feature was added using Google data that can't be exported",SK:"This format will be used to display degrees for Latitude/Longitude.",ss:"This helps calculate carbon emissions and potential financial savings.",xA:"This info was provided by Google. Adding your own description, images, or videos will clear it.",Dg:"This is a label given to the design with the highest score, indicating that the selected design has the highest quality. This is a small, green tag shown at the top of the details page for the selected design. It is only present for the best design from all designs available.",ET:"This layer is currently unavailable in Earth.",Rc:"This layer is no longer supported in Earth.",Ca:"This layer was originally added to a different map and cannot be copied.",v0:"This menu option will display the legal license information for the open source software used in our app.",WU:"This project contains Experimental functionality that is not yet supported.",qq:"This project requires a more recent version of Google Earth.",ja:"This setting determines which view to load by default when opening Earth.",iY:"This text shows on a toolbar when user taps on the pegman icon and the map shows the blue coverage overlay for street view panos. The text is shown below the street view info highlighting the possibility to explore historical imagery in Street View.",Yf:"This text shows on a toolbar when user taps on the pegman icon and the map shows the blue coverage overlay for street view panos. The text is used to inform user that now they can tap/click on a location that is covered by the blue overlay to enter street view.",PH:"This theme will be used for panels, menus, dialogs, and other elements.",Fg:"This will clear the list of trusted and untrusted domains for loading KML content.",PI:"This will clear the persistent cache on this device.",w7:"This will clear the search history on this device.",F1:"Time including microseconds is outside valid range",eE:"Timelapse is a global video showing nearly four decades of planetary change.",jy:"Timelapse mode temporarily disables 3D buildings for optimal viewing.",CX:"Title displayed in the Data Table if the data layer is hidden. This indicates that the data is not visible since the user has hidden the data layer.",Zn:"Title displayed in the Data Table if there are no features visible in the current viewport.",Wp:"Title displayed in the Data Table if there was a generic error while fetching or displaying data for the data table.",vd:"Title displayed to user to allow them to clear the search history on the device.",t_:"Title for a card or bottom sheet that shows the measure tool user interface.",GF:"Title for a data table containing design stats for a generated built environment design. Design stats include metrics like average building height, number of buildings, etc.",MY:"Title for a data table containing metrics about parking areas for a generated built environment design. Example parking areas include surface parking and basement parking.",YW:"Title for a data table containing metrics by building unit type for a generated built environment design. Example unit types include studio apartments, 2 bedroom apartments, etc.",iy:"Title for a data table containing metrics by parcel for a generated built environment design.",G1:"Title for a dialog asking if the user wants to delete the attribute for the current key or delete the key itself.",JI:"Title for a dialog for adding an attribute to a feature.",_3:"Title for a dialog informing the user that an update is required to use Google Earth.",Ms:"Title for a dialog that allows the user to open or create a new local KML file.",lj:"Title for a pane showing completed operations for the current project.",lk:"Title for a pane showing the ongoing operations for the current project.",uJ:"Title for a row within the style editor that lets users edit the colors of points and/or lines within a layer.",ip:"Title for a row within the style editor that lets users edit the fill colors of geometries within a layer.",bL:"Title for a row within the style editor that lets users edit the outline width and color of strokes within a layer.",j2:"Title for a row within the style editor that lets users edit the sizes of icons within a layer.",hD:"Title for a tile that shows advanced measurements, such as elevation.",x8:"Title for a tool that lets the user draw lines or shapes on the map.",N3:"Title for a toolbar that is displayed when Google Earth is showing a photo panorama that does not have an address string.",zK:"Title for an editor row that lets users edit the fill color and opacity of polygons",ZS:"Title for an editor row that lets users edit the outline color and width of polygons",pX:"Title for an item in the Earth Mate onboarding dialog.",hh:"Title for banner to notify users that the current feature is part of a reference project. A reference project is a project the user wants to reference while working on a separate project.",Vj:"Title for collecting user inputs in the Sustainability step. This is located in the design inputs panel for NewBuild designs.",fe:"Title for dialog in user import data layer flow to select output type (data layer or map features).",e:"Title for the Add menu in the menu bar. The ampersand indicates the activation letter (e.g. Alt+A for Add).",Y:"Title for the File menu in the menu bar. The ampersand indicates the activation letter (e.g. Alt+F for File).",X1:"Title for the Help menu in the menu bar. The ampersand indicates the activation letter (e.g. Alt+H for Help).",eY:"Title for the Tools menu in the menu bar. The ampersand indicates the activation letter (e.g. Alt+T for Tools).",On:"Title for the UI that manages the historical imagery feature.",N:"Title for the View menu in the menu bar. The ampersand indicates the activation letter (e.g. Alt+V for View).",q2:"Title for the area showing advanced settings for building use types. Use types refer to how the building will be used (e.g. for residential or commercial purposes).",ye:"Title for the data layer option in the user import output selector dialog.",W2:"Title for the elevation profile chart. An elevation profile is a chart that shows the elevation of a path over terrain. Elevation refers to the height of a point above sea level. It's a profile because it's the view from the side, perpendicular to the path.",mF:"Title for the generated designs pane indicating the status, and that the designs are complete.",Eg:"Title for the image generator feature, which uses AI to modify screenshots.",vz:"Title for the info section that describes the steps for running the design generation tool.",ZB:"Title for the map features option in the user import output selector dialog.",EO:"Title for the map legend, shown in a button if the legend is collapsed or in a panel if the legend is expanded.",ev:"Title in a dialog that appears after the first time a user tries to share their project via Drive.",Gg:"Title label for a card that shows information about a pin that a user dropped onto the earth view",Kv:"Title label for a card that shows information about the user's location",GY:"Title of a banner that is shown when a document feature is restricted from being exported to a KML file.",w1:"Title of a button in the settings UI thast lets the user reset all settings to their factory default values.",IM:"Title of a card shown when there is an error from fetching data for the selected layer feature.",b:"Title of a category divider in the settings UI, used to visually group together certain settings entries.",u_:"Title of a dialog asking the user if they want to allow Earth to load KML content from an untrusted third-party domain.",Bu:"Title of a dialog asking the user to confirm moving a cloud document to the trash.",uv:"Title of a dialog asking the user to confirm whether they want to delete a project.",Cd:"Title of a dialog notifying the user that the Voyager feature has moved outside of the Earth app",Tl:"Title of a dialog that allows the user to choose a plan for their Earth Pro subscription.",ni:"Title of a dialog that allows the user to input a hexadecimal color.",gc:"Title of a dialog that asks the user to confirm that they want to create more designs like this design using the same inputs by going through the design input tool again.",j0:"Title of a dialog that asks the user to rename their project before sharing it.",tg:'Title of a dialog that previews a screenshot the user is about to share and presents a "Share" button to share it.',c9:"Title of a dialog that prompts the user to refresh the app in order to enable their Google Earth Professional Advanced subscription.",_p:"Title of a dialog that shows data attribution information for satellite and aerial imagery and vector map data.",Bn:"Title of a dialog that shows the data layers that are available to add to the current project.",_f:"Title of a dialog that warns the user that some layers and features cannot be exported as a KML file.",az:"Title of a dialog that warns the user that the document cannot be exported as a KML file.",wr:"Title of a dialog that welcomes the user to the Google Earth 'Professional Advanced' plan.",uy:"Title of a dialog that welcomes the user to the Google Earth 'Professional' plan.",VE:"Title of a menu item that allows the user to add an image or video from a URL to a feature.",Fy:"Title of a menu item that allows the user to add an image to a feature by uploading it from a file on their computer.",Mb:"Title of a popup dialog that allows the user to list their Browser KML files.",sL:"Title of a promo card that promotes the use of new features, specifically bulk editing and undo/redo.",u6:"Title of a row in the layer style editor for changing what attribute is used for data-driven styling.",cL:"Title of a search suggestion group which contains a subset of the most recent user searches.",T_:"Title of a search suggestion group which contains any local KML projects that match the user's search query.",YI:"Title of a status tracker indicating that a design is being imported.",V4:"Title of a view that promotes the overhead satellite imagery search feature in the Earth AI assistant.",II:"Title of an overflow menu item for renaming a project.",u0:"Title of the Data tab in the Inspector's layer details view.",c7:"Title of the Energy Use step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",Du:"Title of the Filter tab in the Inspector's layer details view.",wh:"Title of the Financials step of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",NS:"Title of the Site (e.g. a land area) tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs.",xv:"Title of the Site (e.g. a land area) tab of the workflow that surfaces the previous user input for the site used to generate designs.",jb:"Title of the Source tab in the Inspector's layer details view.",iz:"Title of the Style tab in the Inspector's layer details view.",Rm:"Title of the data field dropdown, which is used to select the column to style a layer by.",dQ:"Title of the expandable 'Labels' section of the property editor.",Fa:"Title of the expandable 'Model' section of the property editor. This section allows modification of 3D model orientation and scaling.",He:"Title of the expandable 'Presentation settings' section of the property editor.",E0:"Title of the expandable 'Transform' section of the property editor. This section allows modification of 3D model orientation and scaling.",Jx:"Title of the field to edit the Altitude within the 'Placemark Placement' section of the property editor.",XS:"Title of the field to edit the Latitude within the 'Placemark Placement' section of the property editor.",Vo:"Title of the field to edit the Longitude within the 'Placemark Placement' section of the property editor.",yN:"Title of the label size dropdown, which is used to scale the size of labels within a layer.",ES:"Title of the label size selector in the labels section of the property editor.",YR:"Title text for a tool that allows users to create aspect layers for a given polygon. Aspect is the direction that a slope faces. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",oc:"Title text for a tool that allows users to create contour layers for a given polygon. Contours refer to elevation contour lines, which are lines that connect points of equal elevation on terrain.",z9:"Title text for a tool that allows users to create cut and fill layers for a given polygon. Cut and fill refers to the process of removing and adding soil to create a level surface. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",xV:"Title text for a tool that allows users to create slope layers for a given polygon. Slope refers to the steepness of the terrain. A layer is a collection of geospatial data that can be overlaid on top of a base map.",_e:"Title text in the parking tab of the workflow that collects user input used to generate designs. Targets refers to the target number of parking spots that the user wants to have in the design.",Bw:"To add pictures directly to Earth, allow camera access",mm:"To add pictures directly to Earth, allow photo library access",W8:"To omit basement floor groups, set the min and max floor counts to 0 for each floor group in the basement.",Q:"Toast informing the user that a string was copied to the clipboard.",MV:"Toast informing the user that content was successfully pasted into a document.",S6:"Toast message for a failure uploading a document.",mM:"Toast message indicating a problem writing to the server during an import",au:"Toast message indicating an internal error during an import",ns:"Toast message indicating an invalid Url during an import",hK:"Toast message indicating that a feature cannot be added to the project because the project's feature count limit has been reached.",mH:"Toast message indicating that the document from drive could not be imported",Us:"Toast message indicating that the local document could not be imported",be:"Toast message indicating that the path style has been copied.",od:"Toast message indicating that the path style has been pasted.",cN:"Toast message indicating that the path style has been reset to its defaults.",NW:"Toast message indicating that the placemark style has been copied.",DZ:"Toast message indicating that the placemark style has been pasted.",Gh:"Toast message indicating that the placemark style has been reset to its defaults.",Dx:"Toast message indicating that the polygon style has been copied.",By:"Toast message indicating that the polygon style has been pasted.",D2:"Toast message indicating that the polygon style has been reset to its defaults.",Ln:"Toast message indicating that the style has been pasted.",N_:"Toast message indicating that the user is signed out during an import",g0:"Toast message informing the user that the app does not have permission to access the device camera",J0:"Toast message informing the user that the app does not have permission to access the photo library.",An:"Toast message shown when a user successfully discards a draft design.",Ef:"Toast message shown when pasting some content that does not appear to be a valid KML content",Ix:"Toast message shown when the request to start over with a new draft is in progress.",ij:"Toast message shown when there's an error while discarding previous inputs.",oF:"Toast message shown when there's an error while starting over with a new draft.",dW:"Toast shown to notify the user that only JPEG, PNG, SVG and HEIF/HEIC image types are supported at this time.",ix:"Toast shown when a single feature could not be moved via a drag and drop operation between projects. The 'yet!' is optional, and to indicate that we are aware of this limitation and working to fix it in the future.",IQ:"Toast shown when a single feature could not be moved via a drag and drop operation.",Rp:"Toast shown when the document reached a critical number of features and is nearing the limit.",cR:"Toast shown when the document reached the maximum number of features.",sI:"Toast shown when the document was made with a more recent version of Google Earth, and is not fully supported.",Qi:"Toast text that indicates that the app has successfully created new inputs, which are the values that go in to a process.",HH:"Toast text that indicates that the app is currently creating new inputs, which are the values that go in to a process.",R4:"Toast text that indicates that there was an error while creating new inputs, which are the values that go in to a process. We prompt the user to attempt to do this action again or reload/refresh the website.",Dz:"Toast to inform the user that they are operating without an account.",sx:"Too many requests in a short time. Please try again later.",d4:"Tool name for creating a classification layer. Classification layers use AI to categorize the basemap into different classes based on user-defined sample points.",J1:"Tooltip explaining an informational display in the status bar of the current camera altitude, which is in meters or feet relative to sea level.",qc:"Tooltip for Min/Max number of floors in building type editor",B3:"Tooltip for a back button that allows users to exit Street View",sO:"Tooltip for a back button that allows users to exit Voyager",EW:"Tooltip for a back button that allows users to exit present mode",wu:"Tooltip for a button for downloading design artifacts and data tables, generated geometries, images, and financial models. Clicking the button will show the user a menu of options for the download format.",g_:"Tooltip for a button indicating that the user wishes to hide the table of contents for a project in Present mode.",rL:"Tooltip for a button indicating that the user wishes to show the table of contents for a project in Present mode.",Ki:"Tooltip for a button that adds a floor to a building floor group. Use types are the intended usage of the floors such as residential, office, or retail space.",wT:"Tooltip for a button that allows the user to open a panel that displays all of the built environment design contents for a project.",Cv:"Tooltip for a button that allows the user to request access to a project.",D:"Tooltip for a button that allows users to return to a previous screen or state.",u:"Tooltip for a button that collapses an expanded section in a list.",JS:"Tooltip for a button that confirms the current changes.",Vf:"Tooltip for a button that deletes an image from a feature.",_X:"Tooltip for a button that expands a collapsed section in a list.",Oh:"Tooltip for a button that hides the menu bar at the top of the view.",mc:"Tooltip for a button that indicates the selected built environment design is starred and clicking the button will unstar it.",q6:"Tooltip for a button that informs users that the current document is view-only. Clicking it opens the request access dialog.",w:"Tooltip for a button that lets the user advance to the next entity in a list, or carousel.",u1:"Tooltip for a button that lets the user go back to the previous entity in a list, or carousel.",d1:"Tooltip for a button that lets users share a link with other users.",fN:"Tooltip for a button that lets users share this project with other users via Drive.",fi:"Tooltip for a button that links users to a place to provide feedback.",ot:"Tooltip for a button that locks the date of historical imagery to the newest available.",zy:"Tooltip for a button that marks the selected built environment design as starred.",_2:"Tooltip for a button that selects the next available newer imagery while the Historical Imagery feature is active.",wB:"Tooltip for a button that selects the next available older imagery while the Historical Imagery feature is active.",qj:"Tooltip for a button that shows the menu bar at the top of the view.",Uq:"Tooltip for a button that will collapse the panel containing search results.",mu:"Tooltip for a button that will hide the timeline of Street View imagery.",OJ:"Tooltip for a button that will scroll the timeline to show newer historical imagery thumbnails that are available for the user to choose from.",mq:"Tooltip for a button that will scroll the timeline to show older historical imagery thumbnails that are available for the user to choose from.",zI:"Tooltip for a button that will show a menu for controlling the camera heading and tilt.",PD:"Tooltip for a button that will show the timeline of Street View imagery.",AD:"Tooltip for a button that would show the timeline of Street View imagery.",C:"Tooltip for a button to delete the current feature in a project.",nW:"Tooltip for a button to edit the current feature in a project.",lT:"Tooltip for a button to reload a project.",xj:"Tooltip for a button to start/play Timelapse video content.",NI:"Tooltip for a button to stop/pause Timelapse video content.",N1:"Tooltip for a drag handle that allows the user to resize the panel by dragging, or collapse the panel by tapping / clicking.",N5:"Tooltip for a drag handle that allows the user to resize the panel by dragging.",LE:"Tooltip for a handle on the Projects panel that will collapse the panel.",DE:"Tooltip for a handle on the Projects panel that will expand the panel.",S0:"Tooltip for a main toolbar button that is disabled when user is in a KML file, as site design is unavailable for that type of file.",fz:"Tooltip for a row in the solar financials metrics table in the design details panel, representing the net present value of a solar design. The net present value is a financial metric that compares expected cashflow to initial investment to assess the value of a project.",nE:"Tooltip for a row in the solar financials metrics table in the design details panel, representing the total savings from investing in a certain solar design.",Q0:"Tooltip for a row in the solar financials metrics table in the design details panel, representing the upfront cost of solar panels after incentives (e.g. national and state tax credits, rebates, cash) have been applied. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",XX:"Tooltip for a switch letting the use choose whether the text label for a placemark on the globe should be shown.",DF:"Tooltip for a text field that allows changing the name of a feature or project",J2:"Tooltip for a toolbar button that will disable the Historical Imagery feature",yh:"Tooltip for a toolbar button that will enable the Historical Imagery feature",_n:"Tooltip for a toolbar button that will enable the Historical Imagery feature. This tooltip serves as an onboarding message and will be shown to users who have not used the feature before.",Kl:"Tooltip for a toolbar button to open the available data layers dialog, which allows users to select from data layers to add to their project.",E7:"Tooltip for aggregate stats estimate label explaining why the value is an estimate. A finished drawing is defined as once the user clicks saves project. Inferred data data based on data samples.",j7:"Tooltip for an icon button in the Data Table bottom panel that will close the panel.",SL:"Tooltip for an icon button on the area filter tool that clears the user's drawn polygon and allows them to draw a new one.",UP:"Tooltip for an info icon that, when clicked, opens a help article with more information about storage quota.",S_:"Tooltip for button that opens the project that the current feature belongs to.",pT:"Tooltip for button that shows built-in map layers like borders, roads, labels, photos, etc.",k8:"Tooltip for info button that shows information about layers.",B5:"Tooltip for the Real Estate Clean Energy Development Tools menu option in the Earth main toolbar that describes what the design creation feature will do.",fO:"Tooltip for the button that links to a help article for the Earth Design feature.",bz:"Tooltip for the button that will display Help for the Historical Imagery feature.",Qj:"Tooltip for the corridor width field in the building type editor. A corridor is a passage connecting parts of a building like a hallway. Allows the user to specify the corridor width. Double-loaded refers to a corridor layout where rooms or spaces are accessed from both sides of the hallway, rather than just one side.",o6:"Tooltip for the design details program summary table column header representing the number of entities, like parking spots or apartment units in a site.",CW:"Tooltip for the floor to floor height field in the building type editor.",nC:"Tooltip for the help button that is displayed in the timelapse view.",M:"Tooltip for the help button that is displayed in various panes.",fC:"Tooltip for the lease depth field in the building type editor. Cores are unusable areas of a building, like elevators. Lease depth is the distance from the exterior facade to the core or corridor for this group of floors. Lease describes the actual rentable building area between the facade and the core. Rentable area is the area that can be rented because the area is usable. The facade is the exterior of a building.",Xe:"Tooltip for the loss factor field in the building type editor. Loss factor represents the percentage of space that cannot be used. This is the amount of lost space.",qb:"Tooltip for the scale bar, which shows the distance in world space for a particular size on the screen",VN:"Tooltip header for the Real Estate Clean Energy Development Tools menu option in the Earth main toolbar, which indicates that the design creation feature is new.",ME:"Tooltip indicating why the High Contrast setting is disabled.",Pz:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to Site total under Development program in the Program tab of the Generate Designs workflow. Use types refers to the type of use for a building, such as residential, commercial, or industrial.",Jd:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Building Roof Monthly Lease field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the building roof monthly lease. ",tK:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Building roof cost field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the total cost of installing solar panels on a building roof.",nR:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Debt Fraction field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the debt fraction. ",bk:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Electricity rate escalator field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the rate of increase of electricity rate.",r5:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Electricity rate field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the cost of electricity.",hJ:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Financial assumptions header in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the financial assumptions.",vV:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Lease / PPA assumptions header in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the lease or ppa assumptions. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",rX:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Lease rate escalator field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the rate of increase of lease rate.",GU:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Loan rate field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the loan rate.",Ws:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Net metering preference field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the net metering preference.",nk:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the PPA price escalator field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the rate of increase of PPA price. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",Gy:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the PPA price field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the price of a PPA. PPA stands for Power Purchase Agreement.",Fp:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Parking lot cost field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the total cost of installing solar panels ona parking lot.",z2:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Parking lot monthly lease field in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the monthly lease of the parking lot.",Rz:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the Purchase or loan assumptions header in the Financials tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the purchase or loan assumptions.",Vu:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the emissions change metric for a design in the design details tab.",Wi:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the financials section in the design details panel.",ji:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the front yard setback zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",td:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the maximum building coverage ratio zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",OB:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the maximum floor area ratio zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",pr:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the maximum height zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",rU:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the minimum open space ratio zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",N4:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the rear yard setback zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",Ah:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the side yard setback zoning requirement for a land parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",lo:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the zone information of a parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe that zoning data is sourced externally and only available in English for the US.",wv:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the zone information of a parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the behavior when a parcel spans multiple zones.",u2:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the zone information of a parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow to describe the supported zoning requirements. FAR stands for floor to area ratio. BCR stands for building coverage ratio. OSR stands for open space ratio. Can be translated as their full names.",DO:"Tooltip info displayed when the user hovers over an information icon next to the zone information of a parcel in the Site tab of the Generate Designs workflow.",Xr:"Tooltip message describing the behavior of a checkbox that designates whether the associated inputs are required or not. When checked, the FAR (floor to area ratio) input targets for the use type will be met.",lm:"Tooltip message for the help icon when Map features output option is disabled due to unsupported file formats.",q8:"Tooltip message for the help icon when Map features output option is disabled.",qi:"Tooltip message for the help icon when data layer output is disabled because of an existing pending LRO import.",Oi:"Tooltip message for the help icon when the project is in a shared drive.",Di:"Tooltip message for the help icon when the user has exceeded their storage quota.",ZJ:"Tooltip message for the help icon when the user is not the owner of the project.",uB:"Tooltip message for the help icon when validation for data layer output fails with unknown reason.",z:"Tooltip of a button allowing the user to collapse the card containing the button, which will show just the card header.",B:"Tooltip of a button allowing the user to expand the card containing the button to show its full content, instead of just the card header.",kv:"Tooltip of a button that switches the description editor to HTML mode",TA:"Tooltip of a button that switches the description editor to rich text mode",B_:"Tooltip on a button that allows the user to input a hexadecimal color.",LU:"Tooltip on a button to cancel an ongoing activity, like a file import or design generation.",Bj:"Tooltip on a success icon for a completed activity, like a file import or design generation.",Gi:"Tooltip on a warning icon for a completed activity that has failures, like a file import or design generation, with details available to view.",U5:"Tooltip on a warning icon for a completed activity that has failures, like a file import or design generation.",Su:"Tooltip on an error icon for a cancelled activity, like a file import or design generation.",l0:"Tooltip on an error icon for a failed activity, like a file import or design generation, with details available to view.",kS:"Tooltip on an error icon for a failed activity, like a file import or design generation.",aX:"Tooltip shown for a button that toggles the measure tool on and off.",lH:"Tooltip text explaining how to disable basement floor groups when the basement parking strategy is enabled. A floor group is a configuration for a set of floors in a building.",m8:"Tooltip text explaining that a button will cause a project to become hidden",Xu:"Tooltip text explaining that a button will cause a project to become visible",bT:"Tooltip text explaining that classification layers are year-dependent and that sample points collected by the user will apply to the selected year's map.",GN:"Tooltip text explaining why the basement floor group set is disabled. The basement parking strategy is a strategy for deciding whether to build basement parking for the buildings in this study.",Ty:"Tooltip text for a StepperSideMenuItem widget in the StepperFlowPanel widget that is complete.",Ny:"Tooltip text for a button that allows user to redo a previously undone change to the document, e.g. adding/deleting/editing features.",gK:"Tooltip text for a button that allows user to undo their previous change to the document, e.g. adding/deleting/editing features.",lB:"Tooltip text for a button that displays the current feature in a project on the earth.",zp:"Tooltip text for a button that displays the last selected design in a project on the earth.",Dm:"Tooltip text for a button that hides the current feature in a project on the earth.",N6:"Tooltip text for a button that hides the currently selected design from the map.",VX:"Tooltip text for a button that lets the user choose a background color for the current feature's info box.",LN:"Tooltip text for a button that lets the user draw lines or shapes on the map.",pN:"Tooltip text for a button that lets the user drop placemarks (points with an associated icon) at a pre-specified location on the map.",TU:"Tooltip text for a button that lets the user drop placemarks (points with an associated icon) on the map.",jN:"Tooltip text for a button that opens the left-hand navigation panel on the Home screen.",Z9:"Tooltip text for a button that sends a prompt to the Earth AI assistant.",mb:"Tooltip text for a button that stops/cancels a pending Earth AI assistant prompt.",u7:"Tooltip text for a button that will apply a center horizontal alignment to the selected block of text.",HQ:"Tooltip text for a button that will apply a left horizontal alignment to the selected block of text.",Cc:"Tooltip text for a button that will apply a right horizontal alignment to the selected block of text.",k2:"Tooltip text for a button that will apply an unordered list (like a bulleted list) to the selected block of text.",lU:"Tooltip text for a button that will apply an unordered list (like a numbered list) to the selected block of text.",r7:"Tooltip text for a button that will decrease the horizontal indentation of the selected block of text.",Mc:"Tooltip text for a button that will increase the horizontal indentation of the selected block of text.",MA:"Tooltip text for a button that will remove all formatting (like bold or a custom text size) from the selected block of text.",_B:"Tooltip text for a button that will show a dialog allowing the user to add a link (hyperlink) to the selected text.",t6:"Tooltip text for a button that will show a dialog allowing the user to choose a color for the selected feature.",ZP:"Tooltip text for a button that will show a dialog allowing the user to choose a tint color for the selected feature -- the tint will modulate the pre-existing color.",Nv:"Tooltip text for a button that will show various paragraph styles, like center alignment, bulleted lists, etc.",gt:'Tooltip text for a button that will show various text styles, like "title", "heading", etc.',b2:"Tooltip text for a button that will toggle a bold (boldface) style for the selected text.",ql:"Tooltip text for a button that will toggle an italic (oblique) style for the selected text.",rF:"Tooltip text for a step in the stepper flow panel that has an error.",Uz:"Tooltip text for a step in the stepper flow panel that is incomplete.",V6:"Tooltip text for a step in the stepper flow panel that is unspecified.",eT:"Tooltip text for an icon that indicates that a data layer has a filter applied.",FH:"Tooltip text for an overflow menu button that will show the user a menu of additional items (e.g. a tile overlay or slide) to add to a project.",x:"Tooltip text for an overflow menu button that will show the user a menu of additional options.",GD:"Tooltip text for the Earth AI assistant button when it is first introduced to the user.",Mf:"Tooltip text for the Earth AI button that adds context to the current prompt.",LY:"Tooltip text for the gps button that fly user to a view of his current device location.",YL:"Tooltip text telling the user they can drag a row in a list to reorder it",Fm:"Tooltip text that prompts users to drop a starting point to start measuring a distance or drawing a shape.",SW:'Tooltip to notify users that the app is waiting for designs to be generated. This is shown as a tooltip and accessibility label for the "Generating\u2026" text on the Design Viewer panel when the app does not yet know the number of designs that will be generated.',YY:"Tooltip to show for a label that displays the elevation of the cursor location in the world above sea level",Bt:"Tooltip to show for a label that displays the latitude and longitude at the cursor location in the world",Au:"Total emissions includes all embodied emissions, as well as ten years of operational and transportation emissions. Estimates are based on the design's location, use types, gross floor area (GFA), and building types. Data comes from a variety of sources.\n\nBaseline is calculated by measuring emissions over ten years from the same design that does not incorporate any sustainability strategies.",FW:"Total energy generated based on the solar yield.",os:"Total operational emissions from buildings in this site",eX:"Total power (kW) that can be generated from the recommended solar panels.",QH:'Try asking for overhead imagery, like "find rivers with algae blooms in the US"',FV:"UNDO_REDO_PHASE1_PROJECT_MUTATIONS_ENABLED",ue:"Unable to convert read pixels from SkImage.",Z:"Unable to establish connection on channel.",R_:"Unable to parse the group name. There is no associatedtype or input for this group of designs: ",yH:"Unexpected cancellation. Response from server: ",Xy:"Unexpected data after </kml> tag. Ensure the file ends immediately after the closing tag and try again.",BN:"Unsupported site too large site area state.",_A:"Upgrade storage limit to import additional data layers.",CQ:"Use Historical Imagery and Timelapse to see how the globe has changed over time.",e2:"Use new Gemini capabilities to ask about the map, get data insights, and work faster",Jb:"Use this link or QR code to open Google Earth on another device:",r:"Use type refers to the type of use for a building, such as residential, commercial, or industrial. We set a gross floor area target for each use type.",CO:"Using sustainable materials on your site reduces overall emissions by ",JV:"Value from a boolean (true/false) attribute, presented in popup menu.",k:"VersionNumber must be initialized before use.",Me:"View and edit your local KML or KMZ files all in one place",oI:"View the last 24 hours of cloud coverage in a looping animation.",PQ:"ViewStack map did not contain a widget for view ",_j:"Voyager has moved to a dedicated Voyager showcase on earth.google.com/voyager.",J3:"Want to create a contour data layer? Upgrade now.",Dp:"Want to create a cut and fill data layer? Upgrade now.",jj:"Want to create a slope data layer? Upgrade now.",Mx:"Want to create an aspect data layer? Upgrade now.",sq:"Want to filter a layer by area? Upgrade now.",sp:"Want to select your site using tax lots? Upgrade now.",F0:"We couldn\u2019t get your location. Please try again.",oL:"What do you want to create with map imagery?",CT:"What your site will be used for. This determines which building types you can add to your site.",Ot:"When checked, your FAR (floor to area ratio) input target for the use type will be met. When unchecked, this use type will appear in designs based on the selected building type, without a set target.",qm:"When other people on Google Earth see this project or make edits to it, you\u2019ll be shown as the project owner.",Ci:"When presenting, this feature\u2019s description will be shown as a large panel",xI:"When presenting, this feature\u2019s description will be shown as a small card",KT:"When presenting, this feature\u2019s description will be shown as specified in the KML file",iR:"When presenting, this feature\u2019s description won\u2019t be shown",K:"Windowing APIs are not enabled.\n\nWindowing APIs are currently experimental. Do not use windowing APIs in\nproduction applications or plugins published to pub.dev.\n\nTo try experimental windowing APIs:\n1. Switch to Flutter's main release channel.\n2. Turn on the windowing feature flag.\n\nSee: https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/30701.\n",ex:"XML declaration must be the first line. Move the declaration to the start of the file and try again.",O_:"You are currently offline. Please check your internet connection and try again.",hL:"You can add parking garages when selecting building types for your site.",oB:"You can hold Shift while dragging the Earth to tilt and rotate, or Control to look around.",rN:"You can now evaluate design options for early-stage projects and make more informed planning decisions with rich geospatial data curated by Google.",gd:"You can now expand your geospatial evaluation and decision making with even more designs and rich geospatial data curated by Google.",zS:"You can only view this project. To make changes, ask the owner for edit access.",ZH:"You can select tax lots or draw a custom shape",Rw:"You do not have permission to view this project",lX:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can create a classification layer larger than ",XJ:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can create a contour layer. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",F2:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can create a cut and fill layer. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",KC:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can create a site analysis layer from a larger polygon. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",D4:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can create a slope layer. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",Qu:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can create an aspect layer. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",Lf:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can filter a layer by area. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",jv:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can generate designs for larger sites. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",N9:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can generate more designs per month. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",UH:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can select your site using tax lots. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",Yg:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can use additional data layer. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",G7:"You have access to an upgraded plan where you can view this data layer. Open your settings to activate this upgrade.",Cy:"You have access to an upgraded plan. Open your settings to activate it and get started.",dS:"You need a Google Cloud project to access your upgraded plan. Deselecting this project will remove your access.",US:"You need to be signed in to copy a project in Google Drive. Do you want to continue?",mZ:"You need to be signed in to create a project in Google Drive. Do you want to continue?",Da:"You need to be signed in to open a file from Google Drive. Do you want to continue?",uc:"You need to be signed in to open a project from Google Drive. Do you want to continue?",SF:"You need to be signed in to see Google Drive projects. Do you want to continue?",O2:"You no longer have permission to edit this project",Dn:"You no longer have permission to view this project",el:"You've reached the monthly limit of designs.",YN:"You've reached the monthly limit of designs. Upgrade to generate more.",eP:"You've reached the size limit for your site. Upgrade to increase your limit.",BX:"Your Google AI plan includes higher access to Ask Google Earth.",y9:"Your existing Google Earth projects will not be affected.",KW:"Your import couldn't be completed because it took too long to process. To prevent this, try these tips:\n \u2022 Reduce the number of features in your data.\n \u2022 Simplify complex shapes or geometries.\n \u2022 Remove any unnecessary external images.\n \u2022 Reduce the number of addresses that need to be geocoded.\n \u2022 Import your data in smaller batches.",jX:"Your info will be deleted, but you can always add it again here",Ia:"Your prompt is taking longer than expected. Try narrowing your search or selecting a smaller area.",bM:"Your unit mix percentages must add up to 100%.",Dj:"Zoning data is sourced externally and is available in English for the US.",qn:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] A caption for a button in the generate designs workflow that indicates how many times the user has added a building template card to their design.",aR:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] A label for a subtitle in the lightbox gallery view, indicating the number of images in the gallery, e.g.: 20 images",CB:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] A label for a subtitle in the lightbox gallery view, indicating the number of videos in the gallery, e.g.: 3 videos",bE:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] A message that tells the user the maximum amount of time they should expect a design generation to take.",ZD:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Composition of a bullet point, an error message and a count to be displayed in the Error Guide pane. \u2022 is the unicode representation of a bullet point",_:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Error message displayed in the Error Guide pane following a conversion error during a file import.",dB:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Error message displayed in the Error Guide pane following an error during a file import.",p1:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Error message shown in the Earth AI Assistant chat window when the number of features generated by Earth AI exceeds the limit.",Yl:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Header text for the recommended building templates section in the add building types dialog. The text is followed by the number of recommended buildings.",ii:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Helper text for the area selection tool for classification layers. Classification layers use AI to categorize the basemap into different classes based on user-defined sample points.",PX:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Helper text when a user has drawn an area for a classification layer that is too large for their current plan, but they have access to an upgraded plan. Classification layers use AI to categorize the basemap into different classes based on user-defined sample points.",_R:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Instructional text to describe the cut and fill analysis tool. Cut and fill analysis is a process that measures the volume of earth material that needs to be moved to create a level area of land.",pI:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label describing the number of layers selected in the data catalog.",Hy:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label describing the number of unit mixes for a use type. A use type refers to how the building will be used (e.g. for residential or commercial purposes). Unit mixes are the different types of units that will be in the building (e.g. 1 bedroom, 2 bedroom, 3 bedroom). If a building has 50% 1 bedroom units and 50% 2 bedroom units, it would have 2 unit mixes.",qd:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label for a button that expands an imagery grid to show more images. The count is the total number of images that will be shown if the button is pressed.",sr:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label for a progress indicator that shows the start time and expected duration, in minutes, of a long-running operation.",H1:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label for describing the number of designs displayed in a group when viewing designs by group.",Gu:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label of a menu item allowing the user to specify that the width of a line is a certain number of pixels.  The number will be a positive integer between one and twenty-four, inclusive.  The standard abbreviation for pixels in English is "px", but you can spell out the word "pixel" or "pixels" in your language if necessary for clarity.',Kn:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Label showing the minimum, median, and maximum metrics for a selected area for a feature, with placeholders for the values. Values include the unit. The marker will be replaced by a pipe character. Example: Min: 328 ft | Median: 492 ft | Max: 656 ft",kD:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Message displayed to user indicating that the true value of the slope in percent is greater than the slope value shown. This display should use the appropriate symbol for greater than ">" and percent "%".',Zq:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Message shown in a toast warning the user that a Google Earth project just tried to load content from multiple third-party servers (that is, servers not under Google's control).  Loading content from a third-party server can be dangerous because it lets the owner of that server track the user.",Nm:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Option for filtering by last modified time. Gets all projects that have been modified in the last x days.",Bv:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Screen reader label for a color hue slider. Hue will be between 0 and 360.",hO:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating a size measured in pixels. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "pixel" or "pixels" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the standard abbreviation "px". Typical presentation: "34 px".',oM:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in (possibly fractional) imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) square miles. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "square mile" or "square miles" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "mi\xb2". Typical presentation: "13.5 mi\xb2".',Vh:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in (possibly fractional) square kilometers. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "square kilometer" or "square kilometers", typically "km\xb2" if following SI conventions. Typical presentation: "34.52 km\xb2".',aO:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in (possibly fractional) square nautical miles. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "square nautical mile" or "square nautical miles". There is no standardized abbreviation for square nautical miles. In English, we are choosing to use "NM\xb2" due to its consistency with the abbreviation "mi\xb2" for (imperial statute) miles. In other locales where the imperial system of measurement is less important, you might choose to abbreviate this in some other way, such as by taking the first characters of the words "nautical" and "miles" in the local language. If in doubt, use one of "nmi\xb2", "NM\xb2", or "M\xb2", all of which are common abbreviations, but avoid using "nm\xb2", as this is the SI unit abbreviation for a square nanometer. Typical presentation: "13.5 NM\xb2".',EX:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in acres. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "acres" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, use the international abbreviation "ac". Typical presentation: "468 ac".',Y7:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in hectares. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "hectares" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, use the international abbreviation "ha". Typical presentation: "13.5 ha".',th:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) square feet. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "square foot" or "square feet" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "ft\xb2". Typical presentation: "468 ft\xb2".',HB:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) square yards. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "square yard" or "square yards" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "yd\xb2". Typical presentation: "13.5 yd\xb2".',MJ:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current area measured in square meters. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "square meter" or "square meters", typically "m\xb2" if following SI conventions. Typical presentation: "468 m\xb2".',Pg:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in (possibly fractional) imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) miles. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "mile" or "miles" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "mi". Typical presentation: "468 mi".',Oe:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in (possibly fractional) imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) yards. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "yard" or "yards" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "yd". Typical presentation: "468 yd".',SU:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in (possibly fractional) kilometers. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "kilometer" or "kilometers", typically "km" if following SI conventions. Typical presentation: "34.52 km"',V9:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in (possibly fractional) nautical miles. There is no standardized abbreviation for nautical miles. In English, we are choosing to use "NM" due to its consistency with the abbreviation "mi" for (imperial statute) miles. In other locales where the imperial system of measurement is less important, you might choose to abbreviate this in some other way, such as by taking the first characters of the words "nautical" and "miles" in the local language. If in doubt, use one of "nmi", "NM", or "M", all of which are common abbreviations, but avoid using "nm", as this is the SI unit abbreviation for a nanometer. Typical presentation: "123 NM".',Qc:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in (possibly fractional) smoots. A smoot is an obscure unit of measurement whose name is derived from the name of a person, Oliver R. Smoot. It can therefore generally be transliterated directly into your language's alphabet or syllabary. It need not be abbreviated.",dr:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in centimeters. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "centimeter" or "centimeters", typically "cm" if following SI conventions. Typical presentation: "34 cm".',DT:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) feet. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "foot" or "feet" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "ft". Typical presentation: "34 ft".',FG:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in imperial (a.k.a. British, a.k.a. American) inches. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "inch" or "inches" if one exists in your language. Otherwise, it is probably safe to assume that the user will understand if you use the American standard abbreviation "in". Typical presentation: "34 in".',AK:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current distance measured in meters. This display should use an appropriate abbreviation for "meter" or "meters", typically "m" if following SI conventions. Typical presentation: "468 m".',tZ:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current slope measured in degrees. This display should use the appropriate symbol for degrees "\xb0".',nD:'[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Status display indicating the current slope measured in percent. This display should use the appropriate symbol for percent "%".',rn:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Subtitle of a popup dialog that allows the user to list their Browser KML files, specifying the total number of files being listed.",CS:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text displayed in the bulk property editor when selected features include one or more features that are not part of the current project; the placeholder is a count of the number of features in question.",Ax:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text displayed in the bulk property editor when selected features include one or more features that cannot be edited in bulk; the placeholder is a count of the number of features in question.",Rg:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text label describing the group of features that are currently selected.  This will always be a number greater than one, but please localize all cases just in case this changes.",fo:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text label displaying the number of features in a project that are currently selected.",Zd:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text of a button that allows the user to show the sources of the response. The number of sources is included in the parentheses.",lG:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text of an error message shown when the user has selected more than a fixed number of options in a survey.",CC:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text representing a FAR (floor area ratio) value.",Am:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text representing a percentage value.  This is used in the single design details panel view for the profit on loss metric.",O3:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] Text shown in a dialog asking the user to select up to a fixed number of options in a survey.",Wc:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The category header of a section of building types whose floor-to-area ratio range that is considered high, shown in the add building types dialog. The text is followed by the number of buildings in this section.",uI:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The category header of a section of building types whose floor-to-area ratio range that is considered low, shown in the add building types dialog. The text is followed by the number of buildings in this section.",in:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The category header of a section of building types whose floor-to-area ratio range that is considered medium, shown in the add building types dialog. The text is followed by the number of buildings in this section.",Gk:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included for all designs, regardless of whether sustainability strategies have been applied. It states the total emissions for a design over a 10 year period.",H7:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included only if the heating electrification strategy has been applied to a design. This strategy reduces the amount of energy used for heating by electrifying heating systems.",se:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included only if the reduced parking strategy has been applied to a design. This strategy reduces the amount of parking spaces provided in a design.",Yp:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included only if the solar strategy has been applied to a design. This strategy adds solar panels to a design.",UD:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The description for the design details sustainability metrics table. This sentence is included only if the sustainable materials strategy has been applied to a design. This strategy uses materials with lower embodied carbon in a design.",s6:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The text shown after a value representing the payback period row in the solar financials table in the design details panel. This represents the number of years it will take to break even on the investment for solar panels.",Vx:"[TRANSLATOR NOTE: The numeric placeholders in this message have been pre-localized into the numeral system and decimal separators of the target language.] The value measu